WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:45.754 --> 00:00:50.049
BON APPÉTIT, YOUR MAJESTY

2
00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:52.552
[dramatic music playing]

3
00:00:54.262 --> 00:00:55.764
It is because…

4
00:00:56.598 --> 00:00:57.849
[Ji-young] No way.

5
00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:01.644
[Yi Heon] I have begun to see you
for the woman you are.

6
00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:02.729
[grunts]

7
00:01:04.856 --> 00:01:07.067
It's simply because
I like the food you make.

8
00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:08.735
What?

9
00:01:08.818 --> 00:01:12.572
Wait, why are you turned away from me
when you're saying that?

10
00:01:12.655 --> 00:01:14.574
[stutters] Well, I…

11
00:01:14.657 --> 00:01:16.451
-I mean.
-Hold on.

12
00:01:17.285 --> 00:01:19.412
-Uh, well, so the thing is I…
-Why are you running away?

13
00:01:19.496 --> 00:01:22.373
-[stutters, grunts]
-W-Why are you running… [gasps]

14
00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:25.502
-[screams]
-[grunts]

15
00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:26.795
[romantic music playing]

16
00:01:36.513 --> 00:01:39.140
[both breathing heavily]

17
00:01:47.982 --> 00:01:49.108
It is your fault.

18
00:01:49.192 --> 00:01:51.736
If you had not kept coming towards me
like that,

19
00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:53.988
I would not have fallen over like I did.

20
00:01:54.072 --> 00:01:56.783
Uh, w-why are you angry?
It's okay to fall over, you know.

21
00:01:56.866 --> 00:01:58.368
-[clears throat]
-[sighs]

22
00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:00.120
I'm okay, by the way.

23
00:02:01.246 --> 00:02:04.249
-[sighs] I scraped myself.
-Let me see.

24
00:02:06.584 --> 00:02:07.710
[Yi Heon gasps]

25
00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:10.004
That is more than just
a scrape, is it not?

26
00:02:11.714 --> 00:02:14.592
[blowing]

27
00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:20.306
I will tell the royal doctor.

28
00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:21.599
[chuckles]

29
00:02:21.683 --> 00:02:25.436
Your Majesty, we get minor injuries like
this all the time in the royal kitchen.

30
00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:26.980
I'm really okay.

31
00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:28.731
Oh.

32
00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:30.316
Is that so?

33
00:02:30.942 --> 00:02:33.444
-I didn't know that. [clears throat]
-[chuckles]

34
00:02:33.528 --> 00:02:37.365
I will tell the royal kitchen now
to dull all the knives they have.

35
00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:39.242
No, it's fine.

36
00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:41.578
I found what I needed so…

37
00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:43.705
I will return now.

38
00:02:45.206 --> 00:02:46.708
Now that you've found your bag

39
00:02:47.375 --> 00:02:48.877
you're returning where?

40
00:02:50.545 --> 00:02:51.921
In the bag there's…

41
00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:54.716
[chuckles] Your bag has what?

42
00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.385
The Mangunrok is inside of it.

43
00:03:03.558 --> 00:03:04.601
Huh?

44
00:03:05.768 --> 00:03:07.520
Huh? Where is it?

45
00:03:07.604 --> 00:03:09.188
[gasps] Hold on.

46
00:03:09.272 --> 00:03:11.524
[breathing heavily]

47
00:03:12.775 --> 00:03:14.694
What the… My phone's also missing.

48
00:03:14.777 --> 00:03:18.406
My Mangunrok. My Mangunrok!

49
00:03:18.489 --> 00:03:19.616
Calm down, Cook Yeon.

50
00:03:20.241 --> 00:03:22.285
There was no book inside
when it was found.

51
00:03:23.828 --> 00:03:25.079
Where did you find this?

52
00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:28.249
-Song-jae was the one who found it.
-Song-jae meaning…

53
00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:30.543
Chief Royal Secretary?

54
00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:32.712
[sighs]

55
00:03:32.795 --> 00:03:36.424
[Song-jae] There was definitely no book
in this bag from the time I found it.

56
00:03:36.507 --> 00:03:37.800
Are you sure about that?

57
00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:40.803
Your Majesty, I would never do so much
as lie in your presence.

58
00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:42.805
[sighs] Oh, that can't be right.

59
00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:45.266
I'm telling you,
it was definitely in here.

60
00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:48.144
-If you have it hiding somewhere with you…
-[gasps]

61
00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:50.313
-…please return it right now.
-I told you, I know nothing of it.

62
00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:52.398
If I knew,
I would return it to you right away.

63
00:03:52.482 --> 00:03:54.901
Oh, man, this is crazy.

64
00:03:54.984 --> 00:03:55.985
[Yi Heon] Cook Yeon,

65
00:03:56.486 --> 00:04:00.865
what I think has happened is the book must
have fallen out into the Salgoji Forest

66
00:04:00.949 --> 00:04:03.034
-when your bag fell off the cliff.
-[sighs]

67
00:04:03.117 --> 00:04:04.869
I mean, my lipstick, pouch,

68
00:04:04.953 --> 00:04:07.664
passport, and wallet are all in here,
but the book's fallen out?

69
00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:11.042
I mean, if not that,
why is it the only thing missing?

70
00:04:11.709 --> 00:04:12.794
Think about it.

71
00:04:12.877 --> 00:04:16.673
What would
Chief Royal Secretary gain from hiding it?

72
00:04:17.298 --> 00:04:18.383
[mysterious music playing]

73
00:04:18.466 --> 00:04:21.469
-I don't know about that.
-I told you, it was not me.

74
00:04:21.552 --> 00:04:23.805
[Ji-young, Yi Heon sigh]

75
00:04:24.389 --> 00:04:25.890
What about this then.

76
00:04:26.474 --> 00:04:29.143
After the envoy leaves,
I will send my soldiers

77
00:04:29.227 --> 00:04:32.021
to look for the Mangunrok
in Salgoji Forest.

78
00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:35.984
If that does not work, I will offer
a prize and issue a mandate to find it.

79
00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:38.111
How does that sound?

80
00:04:39.153 --> 00:04:40.905
Do you swear that you will?

81
00:04:43.366 --> 00:04:45.743
Your Majesty,
I really do need to leave here

82
00:04:45.827 --> 00:04:47.578
and go back to where I belong, okay?

83
00:04:47.662 --> 00:04:49.706
I must return to the future.

84
00:04:50.331 --> 00:04:51.374
[exhales sharply]

85
00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:52.583
Right.

86
00:04:53.209 --> 00:04:56.754
Since you so desperately seek this book,
I'll do whatever I can to get it back.

87
00:04:57.922 --> 00:04:59.924
Okay, thank you. [clicks tongue]

88
00:05:00.008 --> 00:05:03.219
Well, I guess I'll have
to wait it out then.

89
00:05:06.306 --> 00:05:07.307
[sighs]

90
00:05:11.853 --> 00:05:13.396
[sighs]

91
00:05:14.314 --> 00:05:15.773
[sighs]

92
00:05:17.025 --> 00:05:20.111
ROYAL KITCHEN

93
00:05:20.194 --> 00:05:22.905
Has anyone heard of seoktanhyang?

94
00:05:23.781 --> 00:05:27.869
They say His Majesty drank this liquor
and said this… [inhales sharply]

95
00:05:27.952 --> 00:05:30.455
"The taste is so sweet and fragrant

96
00:05:30.538 --> 00:05:35.126
that I cannot help but hold it
in my mouth, reluctant to swallow."

97
00:05:35.209 --> 00:05:37.295
-[Bong-sik laughs]
-[Gil-geum] Oh, my goodness. [chuckles]

98
00:05:37.378 --> 00:05:39.922
-All right, all right. Enough of that.
-[sniffs, sighs]

99
00:05:40.006 --> 00:05:41.716
-Cheers to us.
-Oh.

100
00:05:41.799 --> 00:05:43.051
[all] Cheers!

101
00:05:43.134 --> 00:05:44.802
-[Bong-sik laughs]
-[giggles]

102
00:05:48.556 --> 00:05:49.766
[grunts, clears throat]

103
00:05:50.308 --> 00:05:53.019
[Sim coughing]

104
00:05:53.686 --> 00:05:55.730
Uh-oh. Oh, um, you're here.

105
00:05:55.813 --> 00:05:57.356
Ah, miss you are here.

106
00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:02.862
[coughs] Oh, well, well.
If it isn't the chief royal cook.

107
00:06:02.945 --> 00:06:04.655
Yes. I'm a bit late, aren't I?

108
00:06:04.739 --> 00:06:05.740
[Sim, Gil-geum grunt]

109
00:06:05.823 --> 00:06:07.283
-[sniffs]
-Uh…

110
00:06:07.867 --> 00:06:09.619
-Wait, what is that smell?
-Oh.

111
00:06:10.745 --> 00:06:12.580
You weren't drinking, were you?

112
00:06:13.247 --> 00:06:14.290
-Uh, no…
-Um.

113
00:06:14.373 --> 00:06:16.167
-…I don't smell anything. [chuckles]
-[sniffs]

114
00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:19.003
-[Bong-sik sighs]
-Ugh, this is alcohol.

115
00:06:19.087 --> 00:06:20.797
Well, uh, so, Cook Eom

116
00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.924
-actually brewed us some good liquor…
-[stammers]

117
00:06:23.007 --> 00:06:24.509
…so we were just tasting it.

118
00:06:24.592 --> 00:06:25.593
-Right, right.
-Him.

119
00:06:25.676 --> 00:06:27.637
It's uh, it is seoktanju.

120
00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:31.390
I aged it for seven days
and I opened it this morning

121
00:06:31.474 --> 00:06:34.143
so we were only gonna have a drink each.

122
00:06:35.019 --> 00:06:38.898
-[grunts]
-[stammers] Since it's come to this.

123
00:06:39.607 --> 00:06:42.693
Would you also like to try a bowl,
Chief Royal Cook?

124
00:06:42.777 --> 00:06:44.153
He… Uh…

125
00:06:44.237 --> 00:06:47.406
Yes, miss. Uh, come on.
Maybe just a little.

126
00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:49.992
Can you… [stutters] …not hold your liquor?

127
00:06:50.076 --> 00:06:52.995
Uh, no…
Well, it's not like that. [chuckles]

128
00:06:55.248 --> 00:06:57.083
[Ji-young gulping]

129
00:06:57.166 --> 00:06:58.501
-[exhales sharply]
-[taps on floor]

130
00:06:58.584 --> 00:07:02.630
[in Korean] ♪ What on earth ♪

131
00:07:02.713 --> 00:07:07.802
♪ Am I trying so hard to find? ♪

132
00:07:07.885 --> 00:07:12.557
♪ Where on earth ♪

133
00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:15.560
♪ Am I flowing without rest? ♪

134
00:07:15.643 --> 00:07:16.644
[in English] Hold on, hold on!

135
00:07:16.727 --> 00:07:18.062
-[grunts]
-Mmm.

136
00:07:18.146 --> 00:07:21.274
You guys, there's no rhythm going here,
you know? [exclaims]

137
00:07:21.357 --> 00:07:23.734
I start singing, you come in…

138
00:07:23.818 --> 00:07:25.361
-[taps floor]
-…boom, boom, bap.

139
00:07:25.445 --> 00:07:27.321
-Boom, boom, bap.
-[grunts, exclaims]

140
00:07:27.405 --> 00:07:29.782
You're supposed to give… [groans]

141
00:07:29.866 --> 00:07:31.451
[all vocalizing]

142
00:07:31.534 --> 00:07:33.578
[in Korean]
♪ I once saw the end of my life ♪

143
00:07:33.661 --> 00:07:35.872
♪ My heart grew tight ♪

144
00:07:35.955 --> 00:07:37.957
♪ What stopped me from living ♪

145
00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:40.126
♪ Was the fear I had about my tomorrow ♪

146
00:07:40.209 --> 00:07:43.379
-[cooks exclaim]
-[in English] Good God, that reeks, ugh.

147
00:07:43.463 --> 00:07:45.590
[in Korean]
♪ In those long and repeated days ♪

148
00:07:45.673 --> 00:07:47.383
♪ I saw my abandoned self ♪

149
00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:49.343
-[exhales sharply]
-[cooks exclaim]

150
00:07:49.427 --> 00:07:51.387
-Oh, the smell.
-♪ I wasn't there ♪

151
00:07:51.471 --> 00:07:54.682
♪ And neither was my Mangunrok ♪

152
00:07:54.765 --> 00:07:57.768
♪ You must come back home ♪

153
00:07:57.852 --> 00:07:59.145
[funky music playing]

154
00:07:59.228 --> 00:08:00.730
-[Ji-young exclaims]
-[Bong-sik vocalizes]

155
00:08:03.399 --> 00:08:06.611
[Ji-young vocalizing]

156
00:08:08.029 --> 00:08:10.698
[Ji-young]
♪ Where is the missing Mangunrok? ♪

157
00:08:12.950 --> 00:08:16.287
♪ I will go back ♪

158
00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:20.291
BLACK SESAME MACARON

159
00:08:25.338 --> 00:08:26.339
[dramatic music playing]

160
00:08:26.422 --> 00:08:27.757
[sighs]

161
00:08:30.718 --> 00:08:32.428
[groaning]

162
00:08:32.929 --> 00:08:35.598
-[Ji-young, in English] Oh, my head…
-Oh, gosh.

163
00:08:35.681 --> 00:08:37.391
-…hurts so much.
-Miss, are you awake now, huh?

164
00:08:37.475 --> 00:08:38.935
[groans] It hurts.

165
00:08:40.853 --> 00:08:43.189
Gil-geum, what am I doing here?

166
00:08:43.272 --> 00:08:45.024
[gasps] The royal dinner.

167
00:08:45.107 --> 00:08:46.484
Don't worry.

168
00:08:46.567 --> 00:08:49.362
There was an order for Cook Eom
to prepare the royal dinner today.

169
00:08:49.445 --> 00:08:51.155
Oh, okay.

170
00:08:52.073 --> 00:08:55.618
-[sighs]
-Uh, but did something happen to you?

171
00:08:56.244 --> 00:08:58.538
[imitates Ji-young] Mangunrok!

172
00:08:58.621 --> 00:09:02.291
Mangunrok! Oh, dear, my Mangunrok!

173
00:09:02.375 --> 00:09:04.377
[normal voice]
You went like that and started crying.

174
00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:06.921
-Do you remember doing that?
-[exhales sharply]

175
00:09:08.172 --> 00:09:10.633
[sniffs, sighs]

176
00:09:10.716 --> 00:09:11.717
Gil-geum, listen.

177
00:09:11.801 --> 00:09:13.594
So they found the bag and the--

178
00:09:13.678 --> 00:09:16.180
-The Mangunrok was not in there.
-How did you know?

179
00:09:16.264 --> 00:09:20.977
Well, I know because you were really
drunk and you said it a lot of times.

180
00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:23.062
Ah, I see.

181
00:09:23.938 --> 00:09:25.314
[sighs]

182
00:09:27.024 --> 00:09:30.027
Here I was thinking I would finally
get to return home.

183
00:09:30.111 --> 00:09:31.487
[sobs]

184
00:09:31.571 --> 00:09:33.948
-What do I do now?
-Goodness.

185
00:09:34.031 --> 00:09:37.660
What do you mean? You said His Majesty
promised to find it for you,

186
00:09:37.743 --> 00:09:39.537
-didn't you?
-[gasps] What?

187
00:09:40.037 --> 00:09:41.247
I even told you about that?

188
00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:42.540
[chuckles]

189
00:09:42.623 --> 00:09:45.167
You have said it about thirty-six times.

190
00:09:45.251 --> 00:09:46.252
-Anyway…
-[sighs]

191
00:09:46.335 --> 00:09:49.964
…with His Majesty backing you up so much,
I mean, you can find anything,

192
00:09:50.047 --> 00:09:51.591
-you know?
-I don't know.

193
00:09:51.674 --> 00:09:53.676
I-I don't know. I don't know.

194
00:09:53.759 --> 00:09:55.303
[groans] I'm just going to sleep.

195
00:09:55.386 --> 00:09:58.848
Come on, miss. Let's just hang in there
a little longer, okay?

196
00:09:58.931 --> 00:10:01.809
[sobs] Oh, geez.
Where the heck is it anyway?

197
00:10:01.892 --> 00:10:03.060
[Gil-geum] Hmm.

198
00:10:03.144 --> 00:10:04.186
[crickets chirping]

199
00:10:09.650 --> 00:10:11.569
[melancholy music playing]

200
00:10:12.236 --> 00:10:14.405
What are you trying to say, Cook Yeon?

201
00:10:14.488 --> 00:10:17.992
Your Majesty, I really do need to leave
here and go back to where I belong.

202
00:10:18.075 --> 00:10:20.244
I must return to the future.

203
00:10:21.495 --> 00:10:22.496
[sighs]

204
00:10:23.497 --> 00:10:24.498
But where…

205
00:10:25.958 --> 00:10:28.336
do you keep saying
that you'll be returning to?

206
00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:32.506
I do not understand.

207
00:10:35.843 --> 00:10:37.928
CHANG-SEON
CHIEF EUNUCH OF ROYAL FOOD

208
00:10:43.184 --> 00:10:44.310
[Yi Heon] So,

209
00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:48.606
Ming's envoy has said he's unable
to consume the food of Joseon?

210
00:10:48.689 --> 00:10:50.024
[Won-jun] Yes, Your Majesty.

211
00:10:50.107 --> 00:10:53.069
A message from Lord Yoo,
the reception official in Yangju,

212
00:10:53.152 --> 00:10:54.779
has told us that this is indeed the case.

213
00:10:54.862 --> 00:10:57.698
[Min-seong] Judging by their nitpicking
at the carefully prepared food,

214
00:10:57.782 --> 00:11:01.661
saying it tastes bad, isn't it obvious
that they're to demand something

215
00:11:01.744 --> 00:11:05.373
under the pretext that we overlook
the proper treatment of our guests.

216
00:11:05.456 --> 00:11:08.125
Tell me this. What items were sent back
with the envoy last time?

217
00:11:08.209 --> 00:11:11.879
Peregrine falcons, jujube,
horses, sable fur,

218
00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:17.551
some patterned mats, textiles, silk,
and white paper, Your Majesty.

219
00:11:18.594 --> 00:11:20.262
So there was no ginseng?

220
00:11:20.346 --> 00:11:21.347
[scoffs]

221
00:11:21.931 --> 00:11:23.641
I see. That's what it is.

222
00:11:23.724 --> 00:11:26.477
Your Majesty,
what do you suggest we do now?

223
00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:30.815
Why don't we put together some Ming food
that matches the taste of the envoy?

224
00:11:30.898 --> 00:11:32.817
There are Han people
with good cooking skills

225
00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:35.236
in the settlements
for the naturalized citizens.

226
00:11:35.319 --> 00:11:36.320
[scoffs]

227
00:11:36.862 --> 00:11:38.030
Why don't we…

228
00:11:39.782 --> 00:11:40.908
[inhales sharply]

229
00:11:41.534 --> 00:11:42.535
…let them starve.

230
00:11:43.619 --> 00:11:45.663
-What? [gasps]
-[courtiers murmuring]

231
00:11:45.746 --> 00:11:48.791
-Uh, st-starve?
-[courtier clearing throat]

232
00:11:49.625 --> 00:11:50.793
But Your Majesty,

233
00:11:50.876 --> 00:11:54.171
is that not precisely the sort of excuse
they've been hoping for all along?

234
00:11:54.255 --> 00:11:55.423
He is right, Your Majesty.

235
00:11:55.506 --> 00:11:57.675
What if they force us
to buy their shoddy goods again,

236
00:11:57.758 --> 00:11:59.802
like the last time,
if we really let them starve?

237
00:11:59.885 --> 00:12:02.471
How can you manage diplomacy
while gripped by fear?

238
00:12:02.555 --> 00:12:05.599
His Majesty is correct, Ministers.

239
00:12:05.683 --> 00:12:08.811
How about,
we do not allow the worry to take over,

240
00:12:08.894 --> 00:12:11.689
-but instead, come up with a plan?
-[Mun-jeong] He is correct.

241
00:12:11.772 --> 00:12:13.357
-[sighs]
-[Mun-jeong] As His Majesty said,

242
00:12:13.441 --> 00:12:16.277
if we only focus on appeasing the Ming,
we could lose other practical benefits.

243
00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:17.528
Silence!

244
00:12:19.864 --> 00:12:21.031
[Min-seong clears throat]

245
00:12:21.115 --> 00:12:23.701
I heard that they have brought
three cooks along for the journey.

246
00:12:23.784 --> 00:12:26.203
So I am sure
they will not actually starve.

247
00:12:26.787 --> 00:12:28.706
Regardless of what they are thinking,

248
00:12:28.789 --> 00:12:30.541
we cannot afford to give them
the upper hand.

249
00:12:31.375 --> 00:12:32.710
Understand?

250
00:12:32.793 --> 00:12:35.254
[all] Yes, Your Majesty.

251
00:12:35.754 --> 00:12:37.631
Today's meeting is officially adjourned.

252
00:12:38.257 --> 00:12:40.092
Strictly adhere to protocol.

253
00:12:40.176 --> 00:12:42.178
[all] Yes, Your Majesty.

254
00:12:51.353 --> 00:12:52.396
[door opens]

255
00:12:53.022 --> 00:12:54.815
[courtiers murmuring]

256
00:12:56.025 --> 00:12:59.445
Good Lord. What do we think
he is planning this time around?

257
00:12:59.528 --> 00:13:02.907
It would not be right to have guests here
and not offer anything to eat, would it?

258
00:13:02.990 --> 00:13:05.159
-[Won-jun] Exactly my point.
-"Let them starve."

259
00:13:06.577 --> 00:13:09.371
I do have to say,
that answer was quite unexpected.

260
00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:13.584
But, do you think His Majesty
really meant for us to let them starve?

261
00:13:13.667 --> 00:13:15.294
He instructed us to adhere to protocol…

262
00:13:15.377 --> 00:13:16.962
so how about we cook the hamayeon well.

263
00:13:17.046 --> 00:13:19.048
HAMAYEON: BANQUET HELD
UPON THE ENVOY'S ARRIVAL

264
00:13:19.131 --> 00:13:21.175
Of course. [laughing]

265
00:13:21.759 --> 00:13:23.344
Let us get on our way.

266
00:13:23.969 --> 00:13:26.555
Oh, gosh,
what on earth are we supposed to do?

267
00:13:27.223 --> 00:13:30.559
The Ming envoy's procession
has finally arrived at the palace.

268
00:13:30.643 --> 00:13:32.102
Hurry up and prepare the refreshments.

269
00:13:32.186 --> 00:13:35.064
I heard they didn't eat
because they don't like the Joseon food,

270
00:13:35.147 --> 00:13:37.775
so you're going to need
to show off your skills, Cook Yeon.

271
00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:39.985
Wait, what was wrong with the Joseon food?

272
00:13:40.069 --> 00:13:42.780
Wait so, did they really st-starve
the whole way here?

273
00:13:42.863 --> 00:13:44.281
So I have been informed.

274
00:13:44.365 --> 00:13:46.200
I heard that this chief envoy is a eunuch

275
00:13:46.283 --> 00:13:48.619
who is famous
even in Ming for his culinary tastes.

276
00:13:48.702 --> 00:13:51.330
We'll have to pay extra attention
to the food.

277
00:13:51.413 --> 00:13:53.374
-He was a eunuch?
-[Eunuch Yoon] That's right.

278
00:13:53.457 --> 00:13:56.418
The envoy visiting us is one
of their most influential figures,

279
00:13:56.502 --> 00:13:59.463
having raised the Ming Emperor
since his crown prince days.

280
00:13:59.547 --> 00:14:01.382
So one could assume
that he has a refined palate.

281
00:14:01.465 --> 00:14:03.842
[inhales sharply] Hmm.

282
00:14:03.926 --> 00:14:07.304
We should prepare some refreshments
that he has not tried before.

283
00:14:07.388 --> 00:14:09.265
Does such a thing exist?

284
00:14:09.348 --> 00:14:10.516
Yes.

285
00:14:10.599 --> 00:14:14.353
Well, I'm not sure he will love it,
but I did just think of something.

286
00:14:14.436 --> 00:14:15.938
Oh, what a relief.

287
00:14:16.021 --> 00:14:18.816
[exhales sharply] But even so,
there is cause for concern.

288
00:14:18.899 --> 00:14:22.736
Because I've heard the envoy
is a bit of an eccentric in all regards.

289
00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:24.655
I heard that as well.

290
00:14:24.738 --> 00:14:27.783
It has been said that,
under the guise of entertainment,

291
00:14:27.867 --> 00:14:31.453
he brings Ming cooks with great skills
to hold cooking competitions

292
00:14:31.537 --> 00:14:32.955
against all the Joseon cooks.

293
00:14:33.038 --> 00:14:36.041
[sighs] So you have heard
that rumor as well?

294
00:14:36.125 --> 00:14:37.793
Uiju, Pyeongyang, Yangju,

295
00:14:37.877 --> 00:14:40.462
they say that the cooks
in all regions he's gone through so far

296
00:14:40.546 --> 00:14:42.882
were utterly humiliated
before they knew what hit them.

297
00:14:43.632 --> 00:14:44.633
[sighs]

298
00:14:44.717 --> 00:14:45.801
[dramatic music playing]

299
00:14:59.148 --> 00:15:00.774
TAEPYEONGGWAN

300
00:15:03.611 --> 00:15:05.446
You would have had
a hard time coming such a long way.

301
00:15:05.529 --> 00:15:06.530
YU KUN: CHIEF ENVOY OF MING

302
00:15:06.614 --> 00:15:08.198
-[translator 1 speaking Mandarin]
-[in English] However,

303
00:15:08.282 --> 00:15:10.576
I heard that the Joseon food
was not to your liking,

304
00:15:10.659 --> 00:15:11.785
causing you some issues.

305
00:15:11.869 --> 00:15:15.372
[speaking Mandarin]

306
00:15:16.707 --> 00:15:19.335
[speaking Mandarin]

307
00:15:21.879 --> 00:15:23.213
[in English] He claims he didn't starve,

308
00:15:23.297 --> 00:15:25.257
thanks to the Ming cooks
that he brought along.

309
00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:28.928
I trust that they
are astoundingly talented in the kitchen.

310
00:15:29.011 --> 00:15:30.346
[translator speaks Mandarin]

311
00:15:30.429 --> 00:15:32.973
[speaking Mandarin]

312
00:15:34.183 --> 00:15:37.227
[in English] He says that they serve as
both his cooks and as his personal guards.

313
00:15:37.311 --> 00:15:38.354
[speaks Mandarin]

314
00:15:38.437 --> 00:15:41.774
[in English] So, first among
the esteemed Ming dynasty cooks,

315
00:15:41.857 --> 00:15:44.234
this man is the equivalent
of a chief royal cook,

316
00:15:44.318 --> 00:15:46.737
and the last descendant
of the Sichuan Tang Clan

317
00:15:46.820 --> 00:15:49.865
which actually was annihilated
one-hundred years ago for treason.

318
00:15:49.949 --> 00:15:53.911
He is a legendary cook who defeated
all the most renowned inns of China

319
00:15:53.994 --> 00:15:56.538
and claimed all their signboards
as a symbol of his skill.

320
00:15:56.622 --> 00:16:00.042
[Yu Kun speaking Mandarin]

321
00:16:03.796 --> 00:16:07.257
[English translator] He is Tang
Bailong, the master of Sichuan cuisine.

322
00:16:08.550 --> 00:16:09.551
[blows raspberry]

323
00:16:09.635 --> 00:16:11.470
That sounds a bit too much like fiction,

324
00:16:11.553 --> 00:16:12.638
-doesn't it?
-[gasps]

325
00:16:12.721 --> 00:16:14.264
-[Eunuch Yoon clears throat]
-[chuckles]

326
00:16:14.348 --> 00:16:17.643
All right out of
a martial arts novel. Keep going.

327
00:16:18.560 --> 00:16:22.314
Next is Tang Bailong's niece and protégé.

328
00:16:22.398 --> 00:16:26.777
I heard she is a cook who combines
Sichuan cuisine with other regional dishes

329
00:16:26.860 --> 00:16:28.112
to create a new tradition.

330
00:16:28.737 --> 00:16:30.114
In other words…

331
00:16:30.197 --> 00:16:32.783
[Yu Kun speaks Mandarin]

332
00:16:33.826 --> 00:16:36.662
[English translator] Her name is
Ya Feixiu, the fairy of Sichuan cuisine.

333
00:16:36.745 --> 00:16:39.999
[sighs] She'd practically be
a culinary researcher.

334
00:16:41.125 --> 00:16:42.459
[clears throat]

335
00:16:43.585 --> 00:16:45.838
Next is the most mysterious cook
of them all,

336
00:16:45.921 --> 00:16:47.506
known to be a descendant of Confucius.

337
00:16:48.090 --> 00:16:50.509
He is said to be
a master of Shandong cuisine,

338
00:16:50.592 --> 00:16:52.761
one of the four great cuisines of China,

339
00:16:52.845 --> 00:16:56.890
and they say his culinary skills are
as precise as the blade of a knife.

340
00:16:56.974 --> 00:16:58.475
[Yu Kun speaking Mandarin]

341
00:16:58.559 --> 00:17:00.102
KUNG FU FARE:
CUISINE OF CONFUCIUS FAMILY

342
00:17:00.185 --> 00:17:01.270
SERVED TO THE EMPEROR

343
00:17:01.353 --> 00:17:04.732
[English translator] He is Kong Wenli,
the master of Shandong Kung Fu Cuisine.

344
00:17:04.815 --> 00:17:07.443
That's a whole cooking movie
right there, no?

345
00:17:08.152 --> 00:17:09.862
[chuckles, clears throat] Well,

346
00:17:10.362 --> 00:17:11.613
can't say I'm not intrigued.

347
00:17:11.697 --> 00:17:14.700
[sighs] Oh, my gosh. Those cooks all sound
like they're truly amazing.

348
00:17:14.783 --> 00:17:17.745
[sighs] Someone like me,
who studied abroad for a while

349
00:17:17.828 --> 00:17:20.789
does not measure up to any
of the cooks from the mainland.

350
00:17:20.873 --> 00:17:22.207
[both sigh]

351
00:17:22.791 --> 00:17:24.710
[stammers] Are you gonna be all right?

352
00:17:25.878 --> 00:17:28.505
I'm reminded of an old saying.
What was it?

353
00:17:29.131 --> 00:17:31.967
"Often the grandest feasts,
have nothing to eat."

354
00:17:33.218 --> 00:17:35.971
We don't have time. Hurry up
and get outside. Go, go!

355
00:17:36.638 --> 00:17:38.807
[Yu Kun speaking Mandarin]

356
00:17:45.939 --> 00:17:48.817
[in English] He is saying he will use
those cooks to show the meaning

357
00:17:48.901 --> 00:17:50.903
of true flavor to you, Your Majesty.

358
00:17:50.986 --> 00:17:51.987
Thank you so much.

359
00:17:52.071 --> 00:17:53.697
I look forward to it.

360
00:17:53.781 --> 00:17:55.449
Just one thing though.

361
00:17:55.532 --> 00:17:57.701
Tell him that I also have
a chief royal cook.

362
00:17:57.785 --> 00:17:59.703
[speaking Mandarin]

363
00:17:59.787 --> 00:18:01.747
[in English]
Let him know that I intend to give him

364
00:18:02.372 --> 00:18:04.500
a taste of how good
true Joseon cuisine is.

365
00:18:04.583 --> 00:18:05.959
[laughs]

366
00:18:06.043 --> 00:18:08.712
[speaking Mandarin]

367
00:18:14.510 --> 00:18:17.054
[in English] He says he has already heard
about the gwinyeo cook.

368
00:18:17.805 --> 00:18:19.306
[speaking Mandarin]

369
00:18:19.389 --> 00:18:21.100
[English translator]
He says he is curious.

370
00:18:22.351 --> 00:18:24.019
You will soon get to have a taste.

371
00:18:25.854 --> 00:18:27.356
[tense music playing]

372
00:18:28.732 --> 00:18:31.110
-Will you please come inside.
-[translator 2 speaks Mandarin]

373
00:18:31.193 --> 00:18:32.486
[grunts]

374
00:18:43.872 --> 00:18:46.917
[in English] This is the secret weapon
we'll be using for this.

375
00:18:47.709 --> 00:18:48.961
Butter.

376
00:18:49.044 --> 00:18:50.212
[mysterious music playing]

377
00:18:51.171 --> 00:18:52.172
"Batter"?

378
00:18:52.714 --> 00:18:53.841
"Botto"?

379
00:18:53.924 --> 00:18:55.175
"Bulter"?

380
00:18:55.259 --> 00:18:56.593
"Buttu"?

381
00:18:56.677 --> 00:18:58.428
[sniffs] Oh…

382
00:18:58.512 --> 00:19:02.558
Are you sure you can capture the
taste buds of all the envoys with this?

383
00:19:02.641 --> 00:19:06.186
Of course. Everyone knows that
nothing eases the tension like a dessert.

384
00:19:06.270 --> 00:19:08.730
-If it's envoys from Ming…
-[Sim smacks lips]

385
00:19:08.814 --> 00:19:11.066
…well, they'll be tired
from the long journey.

386
00:19:11.150 --> 00:19:13.652
So, sweetness is the way to win them over.

387
00:19:13.735 --> 00:19:15.445
But how do you make this dessert anyway?

388
00:19:15.529 --> 00:19:17.281
So, the way you do it is you

389
00:19:17.364 --> 00:19:19.867
boil cow's milk and collect the residue
that floats to the surface.

390
00:19:19.950 --> 00:19:21.368
[Gil-geum] Oh, right.

391
00:19:21.451 --> 00:19:23.871
I was wondering what you
were making these last few days.

392
00:19:23.954 --> 00:19:26.331
-Ah, so this was it, huh?
-[chuckles]

393
00:19:26.415 --> 00:19:30.252
Ooh. Last time it had a smell of hazelnut.

394
00:19:30.335 --> 00:19:35.132
[sniffs] Ah, this time, it gives off
a pretty tangy yet truly savory aroma.

395
00:19:35.215 --> 00:19:36.884
-[sniffs]
-You're right.

396
00:19:45.893 --> 00:19:46.894
[Yi Heon sighs]

397
00:19:50.397 --> 00:19:51.773
Your point being

398
00:19:52.524 --> 00:19:55.152
that you expect us
to add fifty more tribute women

399
00:19:55.235 --> 00:19:58.155
and also double the amount
of ginseng in relation to last time?

400
00:19:58.238 --> 00:19:59.823
Was it not agreed upon last time

401
00:19:59.907 --> 00:20:02.743
that we would no longer be sending
any tribute women?

402
00:20:02.826 --> 00:20:06.496
-[translator 2 speaking Mandarin]
-So this is truly the Emperor's command?

403
00:20:06.997 --> 00:20:09.875
[speaking Mandarin]

404
00:20:15.005 --> 00:20:17.257
[English translator] He says
he's just upholding the Emperor's orders.

405
00:20:17.341 --> 00:20:18.675
Well, from the sounds of it,

406
00:20:19.635 --> 00:20:22.888
the Emperor has changed his mind
solely on a whim.

407
00:20:22.971 --> 00:20:26.642
Like I told you last time,
we can no longer send tribute women.

408
00:20:27.351 --> 00:20:28.852
As for the ginseng…

409
00:20:31.521 --> 00:20:35.484
I will consider it depending
on what your country offers back to us.

410
00:20:36.401 --> 00:20:38.528
[speaking Mandarin]

411
00:20:39.571 --> 00:20:41.156
[tense music playing]

412
00:20:45.577 --> 00:20:48.747
[in English] He says they will offer their
finest materials, famous teas, ornaments

413
00:20:48.830 --> 00:20:51.625
-and blue and white porcelain.
-No change from the previous gifts.

414
00:20:51.708 --> 00:20:54.920
So they would offer us
the same amount in counter gifts,

415
00:20:56.004 --> 00:20:57.923
while expecting our tribute to increase?

416
00:20:58.006 --> 00:21:01.134
[speaking Mandarin]

417
00:21:04.805 --> 00:21:07.140
[speaking Mandarin]

418
00:21:15.190 --> 00:21:16.858
[oil sizzling]

419
00:21:18.902 --> 00:21:20.946
[sighing]

420
00:21:24.700 --> 00:21:27.661
[in English] Ah, isn't this the suyu
that goes in suyu tea?

421
00:21:27.744 --> 00:21:29.371
SUYU: OLD NAME FOR BUTTER

422
00:21:29.454 --> 00:21:30.497
Suyu tea?

423
00:21:31.206 --> 00:21:32.582
[gasps] Ah.

424
00:21:32.666 --> 00:21:35.168
There was a royal tea named Suyu tea

425
00:21:35.252 --> 00:21:37.671
made by adding butter
to goji berry tea, right?

426
00:21:38.922 --> 00:21:41.633
That's right. Suyu
and butter mean the same thing.

427
00:21:41.717 --> 00:21:42.884
[exclaims]

428
00:21:42.968 --> 00:21:46.888
Uh, so, what are you
planning to make with this suyu?

429
00:21:47.389 --> 00:21:49.850
And what's that sujebi dough-like thing?

430
00:21:49.933 --> 00:21:54.479
You couldn't possibly mean
to add sujebi to the suyu tea, right?

431
00:21:54.563 --> 00:21:56.481
The refreshments we'll be making are…

432
00:21:58.150 --> 00:21:59.151
[chuckles]

433
00:21:59.234 --> 00:22:02.029
[Chang-seon] Your Majesty,
the refreshments have arrived.

434
00:22:02.112 --> 00:22:03.572
[door opens]

435
00:22:03.655 --> 00:22:04.948
[calm music playing]

436
00:22:34.144 --> 00:22:37.064
[sighs, speaks Mandarin]

437
00:22:37.147 --> 00:22:38.774
[in English] He is asking what it is.

438
00:22:41.860 --> 00:22:44.029
This is a macaron, of course.

439
00:22:44.112 --> 00:22:45.363
FRENCH DESSERT MADE PRIMARILY

440
00:22:45.447 --> 00:22:46.823
WITH ALMOND FLOUR,
SUGAR, AND EGG WHITES

441
00:22:46.907 --> 00:22:48.658
"Macrong"?

442
00:22:49.493 --> 00:22:50.994
"Macrong"?

443
00:22:51.078 --> 00:22:53.830
[Ji-young] In the West,
it's eaten as a snack or dessert,

444
00:22:53.914 --> 00:22:56.124
and it is very sweet,
so it lifts your spirits.

445
00:22:56.208 --> 00:22:58.585
[speaking Mandarin]

446
00:22:59.294 --> 00:23:01.630
-[English translator] What is it made of?
-The macaron coques were made

447
00:23:01.713 --> 00:23:04.174
using black sesame, almonds,

448
00:23:06.009 --> 00:23:09.471
butter, egg whites, and some sugar.

449
00:23:11.973 --> 00:23:14.851
These are Joseon-style macarons
made with black sesame,

450
00:23:14.935 --> 00:23:18.438
mugwort, gardenia, jujube, and rice.

451
00:23:18.522 --> 00:23:20.315
[speaking Mandarin]

452
00:23:22.234 --> 00:23:25.654
[in English] What is this thing
in the middle that looks like a rice cake?

453
00:23:25.737 --> 00:23:28.115
That's the filling that goes
in between the macaron.

454
00:23:28.198 --> 00:23:31.326
It's made by mixing butter, sugar,
and black sesame,

455
00:23:31.409 --> 00:23:34.287
and it's a cream filling
with a savory yet sweet taste.

456
00:23:34.913 --> 00:23:36.498
"Creamy"?

457
00:23:36.581 --> 00:23:38.750
Yes. You should try it.

458
00:23:38.834 --> 00:23:42.963
The super crispy texture and sweet taste
of it should help relieve your fatigue.

459
00:23:43.046 --> 00:23:44.464
[translator 2 speaking Mandarin]

460
00:23:47.092 --> 00:23:49.719
[in English]
Now, enough with the explanations.

461
00:23:49.803 --> 00:23:51.346
Please go ahead and try it.

462
00:23:51.429 --> 00:23:53.014
[speaks Mandarin]

463
00:23:55.892 --> 00:23:56.893
[Yu Kun grunts]

464
00:23:57.477 --> 00:23:59.104
[speaks Mandarin]

465
00:24:06.069 --> 00:24:07.571
[grunts]

466
00:24:07.654 --> 00:24:08.655
[sniffs]

467
00:24:19.583 --> 00:24:21.084
[funky music playing]

468
00:24:26.756 --> 00:24:27.966
[exhales sharply]

469
00:24:33.430 --> 00:24:35.599
[sniffing]

470
00:24:35.682 --> 00:24:36.850
Mmm.

471
00:25:05.921 --> 00:25:07.923
[sultry music playing]

472
00:25:14.429 --> 00:25:15.805
[sighs]

473
00:25:17.557 --> 00:25:18.642
Mmm.

474
00:25:32.864 --> 00:25:34.407
[energetic music playing]

475
00:25:36.451 --> 00:25:37.452
[chuckles]

476
00:25:38.495 --> 00:25:40.747
[moans, breathes heavily]

477
00:25:41.915 --> 00:25:43.124
[laughs]

478
00:25:46.127 --> 00:25:47.629
[clears throat]

479
00:25:48.338 --> 00:25:49.714
How do you like the taste?

480
00:25:49.798 --> 00:25:51.299
[translator 2 speaking Mandarin]

481
00:25:53.718 --> 00:25:55.720
[speaking Mandarin]

482
00:25:58.723 --> 00:26:00.725
[in English] He is asking about Cook Yeon.

483
00:26:02.060 --> 00:26:04.437
[exhales sharply] Oh, yes.

484
00:26:05.438 --> 00:26:07.190
That is the chief royal cook I spoke of.

485
00:26:07.274 --> 00:26:10.110
I'm the chief royal cook.
You can call me Yeon Ji-young.

486
00:26:10.193 --> 00:26:12.654
[speaking Mandarin]

487
00:26:15.198 --> 00:26:17.617
[speaking Mandarin]

488
00:26:19.035 --> 00:26:21.496
[in English] He says
Cook Yeon's refreshments are excellent.

489
00:26:23.665 --> 00:26:25.959
[speaking Mandarin]

490
00:26:28.712 --> 00:26:31.589
[in English] He would like to show you
the taste of his great nation too.

491
00:26:31.673 --> 00:26:32.841
Please give it a try.

492
00:26:33.425 --> 00:26:35.635
[speaking Mandarin]

493
00:26:37.887 --> 00:26:39.431
[dramatic music playing]

494
00:26:42.517 --> 00:26:44.769
[in English] He is asking whether
we would like to have Cook Yeon

495
00:26:44.853 --> 00:26:47.772
face off against the cooks of Ming
with our tribute on the line.

496
00:26:48.440 --> 00:26:50.066
[Yi Heon] So, as I heard,

497
00:26:50.150 --> 00:26:52.152
his real intention
is to use the competition

498
00:26:52.235 --> 00:26:54.404
as an excuse to receive a greater tribute.

499
00:26:54.487 --> 00:26:57.240
[Ji-young]
Chinese cuisine is insanely diverse.

500
00:26:57.324 --> 00:26:58.450
A cooking competition?

501
00:27:03.872 --> 00:27:05.999
Tell him we won't do it, okay?

502
00:27:07.542 --> 00:27:10.378
Oh, that is a great idea.

503
00:27:11.087 --> 00:27:13.757
[Ji-young] What are you doing right now?
Tyrant, are you out of your mind?

504
00:27:13.840 --> 00:27:15.091
We aren't prepared at all,

505
00:27:15.175 --> 00:27:17.344
and they came here fully prepared.
Can't you see that?

506
00:27:20.388 --> 00:27:22.557
No, no. No, no, no, no.

507
00:27:22.640 --> 00:27:23.641
No.

508
00:27:25.852 --> 00:27:28.521
Although, since the envoy
has brought three hwabus along with them…

509
00:27:28.605 --> 00:27:30.023
HWABU:
TERM FOR COOK IN ANCIENT CHINA

510
00:27:30.106 --> 00:27:32.192
…why not have the same amount
of cooks from Joseon

511
00:27:32.275 --> 00:27:34.027
compete against them all?

512
00:27:34.110 --> 00:27:36.654
[exclaims, speaking Mandarin]

513
00:27:37.781 --> 00:27:40.200
[Ji-young, in English]
Oh, God. You're killing me. Seriously?

514
00:27:40.283 --> 00:27:42.160
What the heck are you thinking?

515
00:27:42.243 --> 00:27:43.661
A team match? What the…

516
00:27:43.745 --> 00:27:45.455
[Yu Kun speaking Mandarin]

517
00:27:58.176 --> 00:28:00.762
[English translator] He says
the cooking contest should be three rounds

518
00:28:00.845 --> 00:28:02.847
with Your Majesty
and himself as the judges.

519
00:28:02.931 --> 00:28:05.225
[laughing]

520
00:28:05.308 --> 00:28:06.768
What a great idea.

521
00:28:06.851 --> 00:28:08.395
[speaks Mandarin]

522
00:28:09.938 --> 00:28:12.649
[in English]
Well then, we'll decide on the theme

523
00:28:13.608 --> 00:28:15.985
-while we're at the next banquet.
-[exclaims]

524
00:28:21.574 --> 00:28:23.868
[Yu Kun laughing]

525
00:28:23.952 --> 00:28:26.704
[Ji-young] I'm going to go nuts,
seriously. Oh, my God.

526
00:28:28.456 --> 00:28:29.666
Your Majesty.

527
00:28:29.749 --> 00:28:32.919
You can't agree to do such things
without consulting me first!

528
00:28:33.002 --> 00:28:35.755
But did you not signal
to say yes with your hand?

529
00:28:35.839 --> 00:28:37.090
What signal?

530
00:28:37.882 --> 00:28:39.092
Th-This.

531
00:28:39.676 --> 00:28:41.928
No, that means don't do it!

532
00:28:42.011 --> 00:28:43.388
Oh, my goodness.

533
00:28:43.471 --> 00:28:45.098
How could you misunderstand me?

534
00:28:45.974 --> 00:28:49.477
Honestly… You think cooking
will resolve political issues?

535
00:28:50.687 --> 00:28:52.731
Cooking is politics.

536
00:28:52.814 --> 00:28:53.815
Here's the thing.

537
00:28:53.898 --> 00:28:56.985
There's more to politics than weapons,
diplomacy, and documents.

538
00:28:57.068 --> 00:29:00.280
Resolving political issues
by exchanging one another's food cultures

539
00:29:00.363 --> 00:29:01.698
is a very peaceful solution.

540
00:29:01.781 --> 00:29:04.701
How do you expect us to have
a team battle with no preparation at all?

541
00:29:04.784 --> 00:29:07.370
[scoffs] I'm not doing it, okay?

542
00:29:07.912 --> 00:29:09.330
-[sighs]
-"Teem bittle"?

543
00:29:10.331 --> 00:29:11.583
Your Majesty.

544
00:29:11.666 --> 00:29:15.295
Just listen. Can you please just
call off this whole thing?

545
00:29:15.378 --> 00:29:18.381
Could it be…
you do not believe in yourself?

546
00:29:18.465 --> 00:29:22.469
Listen, how could you
just ask me to do this,

547
00:29:22.552 --> 00:29:24.763
and have the entire nation's fate
in my hands?

548
00:29:24.846 --> 00:29:26.055
I think that's totally unfair.

549
00:29:26.139 --> 00:29:28.600
I have recognized you
as the best cook in Joseon.

550
00:29:28.683 --> 00:29:30.393
Who else but you could do it?

551
00:29:30.477 --> 00:29:33.980
Please, just give it your best and try
for me and the people of this nation.

552
00:29:34.063 --> 00:29:36.816
[sighs] This is pushing me to my limit.

553
00:29:37.525 --> 00:29:41.196
I don't understand, why do I have to do it
for the people of this nation, though?

554
00:29:41.279 --> 00:29:43.072
You are the chief royal cook of Joseon.

555
00:29:43.156 --> 00:29:44.365
Tell me what makes you think that

556
00:29:44.449 --> 00:29:46.785
-saving the people is unrelated to you?
-[sighs]

557
00:29:47.285 --> 00:29:48.411
And what do we do if I lose?

558
00:29:48.495 --> 00:29:51.206
You would be a traitor to the nation.

559
00:29:51.289 --> 00:29:54.709
So you're telling me
to put my life on the line once again

560
00:29:54.793 --> 00:29:56.795
for a competition
I am not prepared for at all?

561
00:29:56.878 --> 00:29:59.297
Also, refusing to contend
in the competition with Ming

562
00:29:59.380 --> 00:30:01.007
would be considered treason.

563
00:30:02.425 --> 00:30:05.178
Requests demanding the immediate
punishment of the chief royal cook

564
00:30:05.261 --> 00:30:07.263
-would flood in until…
-[sighs]

565
00:30:07.347 --> 00:30:09.724
As a result… Tsk, tsk.

566
00:30:09.808 --> 00:30:11.684
I mean, you are practically saying

567
00:30:11.768 --> 00:30:14.395
I will not survive if I either refuse
the competition, or lose.

568
00:30:14.479 --> 00:30:17.398
-[chuckles] You finally understand.
-[gasps]

569
00:30:18.525 --> 00:30:20.693
Wow. [chuckles]

570
00:30:20.777 --> 00:30:24.781
So you are pretty much saying I have
to win, without any time to prepare.

571
00:30:24.864 --> 00:30:27.408
Did Seonjo, the cook of the Tang Dynasty,

572
00:30:27.492 --> 00:30:29.828
become the first hwabu
just by making good food?

573
00:30:29.911 --> 00:30:31.204
A true cook does not blame time.

574
00:30:31.287 --> 00:30:34.457
Instead they carefully select ingredients
with intention.

575
00:30:34.541 --> 00:30:36.209
Then they can create a masterpiece.

576
00:30:36.292 --> 00:30:40.088
Yes, but, you can not keep telling me
to risk my life over and over.

577
00:30:40.171 --> 00:30:41.339
Hmm.

578
00:30:41.923 --> 00:30:44.509
I don't think I can do it. [sighs]

579
00:30:46.386 --> 00:30:47.929
If you win the competition,

580
00:30:49.097 --> 00:30:52.058
The Mangunrok…
I'll definitely find it for you.

581
00:30:52.559 --> 00:30:55.603
Huh? That's something
you already promised.

582
00:30:55.687 --> 00:30:57.355
You said you would find it
and let me leave.

583
00:30:57.438 --> 00:30:58.857
I said I would find it for you,

584
00:30:58.940 --> 00:31:01.025
but I never said that
I would let you return to the future.

585
00:31:01.109 --> 00:31:04.362
[stammering] Why are you saying that?

586
00:31:04.445 --> 00:31:05.446
What do you mean?

587
00:31:11.119 --> 00:31:12.328
You must win.

588
00:31:13.997 --> 00:31:15.456
No matter what.

589
00:31:16.708 --> 00:31:17.834
[sighs]

590
00:31:18.334 --> 00:31:20.253
[Inju]
You mean to say that cooks from Ming

591
00:31:20.336 --> 00:31:23.172
will be having a competition
with the cooks of Joseon?

592
00:31:23.256 --> 00:31:25.049
Yes, Your Royal Highness.

593
00:31:25.717 --> 00:31:27.427
Then what are we to do about this?

594
00:31:27.510 --> 00:31:30.763
Just as I was beginning
to enjoy the peace.

595
00:31:30.847 --> 00:31:35.768
His Majesty's rash actions have created
a serious issue for our nation.

596
00:31:35.852 --> 00:31:40.148
How could the cooking skills of the chief
royal cook decide our nation's fate?

597
00:31:40.231 --> 00:31:43.401
Even though Cook Yeon is outstanding
at what she does,

598
00:31:43.484 --> 00:31:46.863
there's no guaranteeing she will win
against the best cooks of Ming.

599
00:31:46.946 --> 00:31:48.156
Hmm.

600
00:31:48.239 --> 00:31:53.161
We must come up with a plan immediately
before the situation only gets worse.

601
00:31:53.745 --> 00:31:55.038
Yes, what kind of plan?

602
00:31:55.121 --> 00:31:59.626
The envoy's name I hear
is Yu Kun, correct? Also a eunuch, right?

603
00:31:59.709 --> 00:32:01.961
-Yes, so I've been told.
-[scoffs]

604
00:32:02.879 --> 00:32:05.590
Seeing as how improperly
he is treating us,

605
00:32:05.673 --> 00:32:10.470
evidently he doesn't understand the
rapport between the royal family and me.

606
00:32:10.553 --> 00:32:12.597
I am going to give you a letter.

607
00:32:13.306 --> 00:32:15.725
Please send it
to the royal family of Ming.

608
00:32:15.808 --> 00:32:18.937
Yes, it would be my honor,
Your Royal Highness.

609
00:32:20.897 --> 00:32:22.148
[sighs]

610
00:32:22.899 --> 00:32:27.111
These are the refreshments that the Ming
envoys got to enjoy today. Let us try.

611
00:32:47.256 --> 00:32:49.050
[both gasp]

612
00:32:54.263 --> 00:32:58.226
Indeed, she does have extraordinary skill!

613
00:32:58.309 --> 00:33:01.354
-Her sunchae dish was also exquisite.
-Mmm.

614
00:33:02.855 --> 00:33:05.274
That is too sweet for me,
I can not eat it.

615
00:33:05.358 --> 00:33:07.902
What are we to do
if she ruins the cooking competition

616
00:33:07.986 --> 00:33:10.154
with Ming with such mediocre skills?

617
00:33:10.238 --> 00:33:13.282
We will have to elect another cook
instead of the chief royal cook.

618
00:33:13.366 --> 00:33:15.618
Who? Who do you suggest?

619
00:33:16.369 --> 00:33:19.414
Why are you making such a fuss just
because you cannot get rid of a cook?

620
00:33:19.497 --> 00:33:21.582
You must refrain
from causing disturbances.

621
00:33:21.666 --> 00:33:23.543
Just wait
until we've carried out the plan.

622
00:33:23.626 --> 00:33:24.877
-However--
-[inhales sharply]

623
00:33:24.961 --> 00:33:25.962
Listen to what I say.

624
00:33:26.921 --> 00:33:31.300
[clears throat] If you wait, then someday,
I will give you that wench as a gift.

625
00:33:32.176 --> 00:33:33.886
Yes, Your Highness.

626
00:33:33.970 --> 00:33:37.348
Through this competition,
His Majesty will suffer a major setback,

627
00:33:37.432 --> 00:33:40.309
and director Yu Kun, having obtained
the ginseng mining rights,

628
00:33:40.393 --> 00:33:44.063
will provide us with the grounds
to reshape the sky of Joseon.

629
00:33:44.731 --> 00:33:47.859
It is His Majesty's own fault
for impulsively accepting

630
00:33:48.693 --> 00:33:51.237
Yu Kun's cooking competition.

631
00:33:53.573 --> 00:33:55.533
Everything's working out for us.

632
00:33:55.616 --> 00:33:58.036
It is unlikely that
her skills will be enough

633
00:33:58.119 --> 00:34:00.455
to compete
against the best cooks from Ming.

634
00:34:01.831 --> 00:34:04.208
Although she seems
to have luck on her side.

635
00:34:04.292 --> 00:34:07.462
I wonder how things will turn out
if His Majesty helps her.

636
00:34:09.297 --> 00:34:11.382
His Majesty can try as hard as he wants.

637
00:34:11.466 --> 00:34:15.511
However, Cook Yeon will never
be able to win that competition.

638
00:34:15.595 --> 00:34:21.350
[chuckles] That makes me suddenly
look forward to the competition with Ming.

639
00:34:21.934 --> 00:34:23.144
[chuckles]

640
00:34:25.730 --> 00:34:28.441
[in Mandarin]
This is from Grand Prince Jesan.

641
00:34:30.109 --> 00:34:35.323
Is there something
you wish to say to me in private?

642
00:34:35.406 --> 00:34:37.200
His Majesty

643
00:34:38.034 --> 00:34:39.869
is not of sound mind.

644
00:34:39.952 --> 00:34:41.746
He often has fits

645
00:34:41.829 --> 00:34:44.207
and even sees things that are not there.

646
00:34:44.290 --> 00:34:45.416
Oh, dear.

647
00:34:46.250 --> 00:34:47.752
Is this really true?

648
00:34:47.835 --> 00:34:49.504
Whenever he has a fit,

649
00:34:49.587 --> 00:34:51.881
he causes strange incidents
that negatively impact the court,

650
00:34:51.964 --> 00:34:54.092
so Joseon must resolve this issue
as soon as possible.

651
00:34:54.175 --> 00:34:58.179
Please relay this

652
00:34:58.262 --> 00:35:01.682
to the Emperor.

653
00:35:01.766 --> 00:35:04.143
Are you saying you wish

654
00:35:05.144 --> 00:35:06.604
to change your ruler?

655
00:35:08.648 --> 00:35:12.902
Then what do I stand to gain from this?

656
00:35:12.985 --> 00:35:15.154
-[laughs]
-I will ensure

657
00:35:15.238 --> 00:35:17.156
that you win the cooking competition,

658
00:35:17.240 --> 00:35:20.201
so set the stakes high.

659
00:35:20.284 --> 00:35:23.704
Instead of 50, demand 100 tribute women.

660
00:35:23.788 --> 00:35:26.958
Instead of demanding
double the amount of ginseng,

661
00:35:27.041 --> 00:35:31.796
demand the right
to harvest all the ginseng in Joseon.

662
00:35:32.380 --> 00:35:36.008
The thought alone pleases me greatly.

663
00:35:36.968 --> 00:35:39.053
[laughing]

664
00:35:39.637 --> 00:35:40.638
However,

665
00:35:40.721 --> 00:35:44.308
it is a given that the greatest cooks
of the Ming will win the competition.

666
00:35:44.392 --> 00:35:47.520
How do you plan to help with that?

667
00:35:47.603 --> 00:35:51.941
My lord, the chief royal cook of Joseon
is incredibly skilled.

668
00:35:52.024 --> 00:35:57.405
You tasted her food yourself,
so you must know.

669
00:35:58.489 --> 00:36:00.074
What if I refuse?

670
00:36:03.202 --> 00:36:06.831
This is a record we kept

671
00:36:06.914 --> 00:36:12.628
of all the gifts you received
and the dates they were received.

672
00:36:13.212 --> 00:36:17.300
Lord Sung! Are you threatening me,
the Emperor's envoy?

673
00:36:17.383 --> 00:36:19.427
I would not dare to.

674
00:36:20.219 --> 00:36:23.431
I will leave this here.

675
00:36:27.560 --> 00:36:32.607
Considering our long-standing ties,

676
00:36:32.690 --> 00:36:35.735
I trust that you will help us.

677
00:36:39.488 --> 00:36:41.532
Our long-standing ties, you say?

678
00:36:42.033 --> 00:36:43.492
[chuckles]

679
00:37:00.509 --> 00:37:05.139
[laughs] He is one sneaky old man.

680
00:37:05.223 --> 00:37:08.017
Seeing how the officials who serve
one king are divided in their loyalties,

681
00:37:08.684 --> 00:37:11.604
it seems that this nation
is nearing its end as well.

682
00:37:12.521 --> 00:37:14.315
What do you mean by that?

683
00:37:14.398 --> 00:37:16.150
It is none of your concern.

684
00:37:16.234 --> 00:37:21.405
It seems that Joseon's chief royal cook
is greatly skilled.

685
00:37:21.489 --> 00:37:23.532
Are you referring
to the refreshment, my lord?

686
00:37:24.200 --> 00:37:26.202
That was just a petty trick.

687
00:37:26.285 --> 00:37:27.995
That does not mean she can truly--

688
00:37:28.079 --> 00:37:29.538
Every competition must be taken seriously.

689
00:37:30.456 --> 00:37:32.792
The pride of our great nation is at stake.

690
00:37:35.044 --> 00:37:38.798
Petty trick or not,

691
00:37:38.881 --> 00:37:41.092
I have to say I am quite curious

692
00:37:41.676 --> 00:37:45.888
as to how skilled the cooks of Joseon are.

693
00:37:46.472 --> 00:37:48.224
How about I test them?

694
00:37:48.307 --> 00:37:50.726
-Ya Feixiu!
-No, Bailong.

695
00:37:51.394 --> 00:37:52.687
Yes, my lord.

696
00:37:53.271 --> 00:37:54.939
We must take this competition
as an opportunity

697
00:37:55.022 --> 00:37:58.192
to humiliate and discourage
the Joseon king.

698
00:37:58.818 --> 00:38:01.153
Will you have a go?

699
00:38:02.071 --> 00:38:03.281
Leave it to me, my lord.

700
00:38:13.666 --> 00:38:14.792
[grunts]

701
00:38:16.919 --> 00:38:18.796
[in English] Whoa, she almost got me.

702
00:38:19.839 --> 00:38:21.507
[grunts, panting]

703
00:38:21.590 --> 00:38:23.551
-[in Mandarin] After him! [panting]
-Yes!

704
00:38:29.098 --> 00:38:30.599
GONG-GIL YEONHUIGUN'S
JESTER WITH MANY SECRETS

705
00:38:30.683 --> 00:38:33.519
[in English] Oh, wow.
They actually feel my presence?

706
00:38:33.602 --> 00:38:35.730
That's very disturbing.

707
00:38:38.858 --> 00:38:40.401
Are they truly that skilled?

708
00:38:40.484 --> 00:38:43.654
Yes. They're more
than just cooks, it seems.

709
00:38:43.738 --> 00:38:44.864
[sighs]

710
00:38:45.906 --> 00:38:46.949
Hold on…

711
00:38:48.659 --> 00:38:50.870
You saw the Imperial Director
there as well?

712
00:38:54.457 --> 00:38:57.168
You spoke with them? The Ming envoy?

713
00:38:57.668 --> 00:38:59.086
Did everything go well?

714
00:38:59.170 --> 00:39:02.048
Yes, Your Highness. You need not worry.

715
00:39:02.131 --> 00:39:03.841
It was merely an exchange of words.

716
00:39:03.924 --> 00:39:06.385
How can you be so sure he can be trusted?

717
00:39:06.469 --> 00:39:09.722
Yu Kun is beyond cunning, Your Highness.

718
00:39:09.805 --> 00:39:12.683
This is the second volume
of Yu Kun's secret ledger.

719
00:39:12.767 --> 00:39:14.894
The first volume I left with Yu Kun.

720
00:39:15.519 --> 00:39:16.896
Well done.

721
00:39:16.979 --> 00:39:20.483
But I fear the consequences
of handing over

722
00:39:20.566 --> 00:39:22.276
the rights to all
of Joseon's ginseng mines--

723
00:39:22.360 --> 00:39:23.402
Right now

724
00:39:24.320 --> 00:39:28.240
is the time to guard Joseon's lifeline,
even if it means sacrificing an arm.

725
00:39:28.324 --> 00:39:30.201
The royal family must stand tall

726
00:39:31.035 --> 00:39:33.788
-in order for the nation to stand tall.
-That is right.

727
00:39:33.871 --> 00:39:39.210
It is a small sacrifice we make here
to save the ancestral rites of Joseon.

728
00:39:39.293 --> 00:39:40.836
And so it is set.

729
00:39:40.920 --> 00:39:44.799
If everyone's made their decision,
we must move forward without hesitation,

730
00:39:44.882 --> 00:39:50.304
to ensure that the Ming cooks, no matter
what happens, win the competition.

731
00:39:50.888 --> 00:39:54.392
I ask that you give
the utmost effort in this task.

732
00:39:55.017 --> 00:39:56.435
This competition

733
00:39:56.519 --> 00:39:59.855
is going to be the starting point
of Joseon's new dynasty.

734
00:40:01.565 --> 00:40:02.858
No matter what.

735
00:40:02.942 --> 00:40:06.404
[Yang-son] The time will come
when that draft will be used.

736
00:40:06.487 --> 00:40:07.613
[Jesan] Indeed.

737
00:40:09.490 --> 00:40:11.575
It quickly approaches.

738
00:40:14.620 --> 00:40:17.498
The bisang you were given,
how did you use it?

739
00:40:18.582 --> 00:40:20.835
I've tried, from the time
of the jinhu until now,

740
00:40:21.460 --> 00:40:24.463
but the royal kitchen has been so busy,
I've had no time.

741
00:40:24.547 --> 00:40:25.840
Of course you didn't.

742
00:40:27.174 --> 00:40:29.844
No man has died without making excuses.

743
00:40:29.927 --> 00:40:33.305
The royal kitchen will face the Ming
hwabus in a cooking competition soon.

744
00:40:35.266 --> 00:40:36.892
A cooking competition?

745
00:40:38.227 --> 00:40:40.563
Yes. You will compete in it.

746
00:40:40.646 --> 00:40:42.356
I shall see to it that you do.

747
00:40:42.440 --> 00:40:46.026
Yes, I will do everything in my power
to uphold the honor of the royal kitchen!

748
00:40:46.110 --> 00:40:47.695
How sweet. No.

749
00:40:48.654 --> 00:40:51.157
Joseon must lose this competition.
Understand?

750
00:40:52.575 --> 00:40:53.576
What?

751
00:40:55.911 --> 00:40:57.121
[chuckles]

752
00:41:00.875 --> 00:41:02.710
[grunts, sniffs]

753
00:41:02.793 --> 00:41:05.421
Don't rub your eyes after touching these,
or you'll be really sorry.

754
00:41:05.504 --> 00:41:10.801
We've spent all day removing these seeds
and pulling the stems off these, but why?

755
00:41:10.885 --> 00:41:12.052
[yelps]

756
00:41:12.136 --> 00:41:14.805
Why didn't you warn me sooner? [shouts]

757
00:41:14.889 --> 00:41:17.308
What are you even going to use these for?

758
00:41:17.391 --> 00:41:19.143
First we dry them like this,

759
00:41:19.226 --> 00:41:22.438
and we ferment them into a paste,
by turning it into a powder.

760
00:41:22.521 --> 00:41:25.441
They say this is so spicy,
you can die from eating it.

761
00:41:25.524 --> 00:41:27.526
And we'll be trying
to make a paste out of it?

762
00:41:27.610 --> 00:41:29.153
So once it's been dried it'll be edible.

763
00:41:29.236 --> 00:41:32.156
-You sure about that?
-Oh, jeez. [grunts]

764
00:41:33.782 --> 00:41:36.577
It's not poisonous.
You can even eat it like this.

765
00:41:36.660 --> 00:41:39.330
[Gil-geum] Mmm!
Did you all see what she just did?

766
00:41:39.413 --> 00:41:42.917
If she says this is the ace up our sleeve
to win the contest then that's what it is.

767
00:41:43.000 --> 00:41:44.168
Now hurry up! Move those fingers.

768
00:41:44.251 --> 00:41:46.128
-That's it. Attagirl.
-[Gil-geum] Chop, chop!

769
00:41:46.712 --> 00:41:48.297
-Goodness, Man-su.
-How is it?

770
00:41:51.842 --> 00:41:53.302
Bet it's too spicy.

771
00:41:53.385 --> 00:41:54.887
-[grunts]
-[Gil-geum laughing]

772
00:41:55.638 --> 00:41:57.097
[gags]

773
00:41:57.181 --> 00:41:59.517
-[Eunuch Yoon] How are we all doing?
-[Gil-geum] Oh, no.

774
00:41:59.600 --> 00:42:01.894
[Bong-sik, strained]
Oh, Eunuch Yoon, what brings you here?

775
00:42:02.436 --> 00:42:05.814
Cook Yeon, His Majesty wishes
to speak with you at once.

776
00:42:05.898 --> 00:42:07.775
Is it about my request
for the travel badge?

777
00:42:08.442 --> 00:42:10.486
You will know after you speak with him.

778
00:42:11.529 --> 00:42:12.613
Sure.

779
00:42:16.867 --> 00:42:18.285
Your Majesty.

780
00:42:20.162 --> 00:42:21.247
[Yi Heon clears throat]

781
00:42:23.958 --> 00:42:24.959
So,

782
00:42:26.126 --> 00:42:27.378
you requested a badge for travel?

783
00:42:27.461 --> 00:42:28.546
Yes.

784
00:42:28.629 --> 00:42:30.673
I'm making a new sauce
for the competition.

785
00:42:30.756 --> 00:42:33.300
But it's hard, so I'd like
to explain it to the miller myself.

786
00:42:33.384 --> 00:42:36.679
Miller? Well then,
are you going to Unjongga?

787
00:42:36.762 --> 00:42:37.972
Uh, yes.

788
00:42:39.473 --> 00:42:41.016
Well, if you must.

789
00:42:41.684 --> 00:42:42.810
Then I'm going with you.

790
00:42:42.893 --> 00:42:45.271
What? Uh… You're going to come too?

791
00:42:46.355 --> 00:42:50.150
Uh… Is it okay for you
to leave the palace for no reason?

792
00:42:50.234 --> 00:42:51.569
What do you mean, no reason?

793
00:42:51.652 --> 00:42:55.447
You need the sauce for the competition.
Can you not think of anything more urgent?

794
00:42:55.531 --> 00:42:57.783
Um, you have a point there.

795
00:42:57.866 --> 00:42:58.951
[grunts]

796
00:42:59.743 --> 00:43:01.620
Hurry along and get yourself changed.

797
00:43:01.704 --> 00:43:04.832
I… I wasn't planning on changing.
I'll wait outside until you're ready.

798
00:43:04.915 --> 00:43:05.916
Hold on.

799
00:43:06.000 --> 00:43:08.043
Do you mean to walk
around the market place

800
00:43:08.127 --> 00:43:10.004
in your chief royal cook uniform?

801
00:43:10.087 --> 00:43:11.171
Well…

802
00:43:11.255 --> 00:43:13.882
Absolutely not, you have
to change into a disguise outfit.

803
00:43:13.966 --> 00:43:15.467
Disguise outfit?

804
00:43:15.551 --> 00:43:18.637
Uh, I could put on Gil-geum's clothes,
she won't mind.

805
00:43:18.721 --> 00:43:20.806
-I used to wear them all the time.
-[sighs]

806
00:43:20.889 --> 00:43:22.391
This is pathetic.

807
00:43:23.183 --> 00:43:25.728
Tsk, tsk. Follow me.

808
00:43:26.645 --> 00:43:27.646
Chang-seon.

809
00:43:57.593 --> 00:43:58.594
[sighs]

810
00:44:28.165 --> 00:44:29.375
[sighs]

811
00:44:30.334 --> 00:44:31.794
[chuckles]

812
00:44:31.877 --> 00:44:33.212
[clears throat]

813
00:44:34.755 --> 00:44:37.508
Is this all really necessary?

814
00:44:37.591 --> 00:44:39.343
We're only going to the mill and back.

815
00:44:39.426 --> 00:44:40.552
I'll be at Gyemumun's front gate.

816
00:44:40.636 --> 00:44:42.179
GYEMUMUN: SMALL GATE NEXT
TO BONGDEOKGUNG'S NORTH GATE

817
00:44:42.262 --> 00:44:44.973
[Ji-young] Huh? Oh, uh, where is that?

818
00:44:47.393 --> 00:44:48.394
I mean…

819
00:44:48.477 --> 00:44:49.770
[door opens]

820
00:44:56.443 --> 00:44:57.528
[Yi Heon clears throat]

821
00:45:01.323 --> 00:45:02.324
Let us go.

822
00:45:07.704 --> 00:45:09.957
[merchant]
We also sell radishes by the half.

823
00:45:10.749 --> 00:45:12.251
We have those as well, ma'am.

824
00:45:13.377 --> 00:45:14.670
[Ji-young giggles]

825
00:45:21.510 --> 00:45:23.011
[no audible dialogue]

826
00:45:26.140 --> 00:45:28.767
Wow, all of these colors are so pretty.

827
00:45:28.851 --> 00:45:30.018
[gasps]

828
00:45:30.811 --> 00:45:33.313
[merchant 2] Oh, my dear, come this way.

829
00:45:33.397 --> 00:45:35.732
Take a gander. [laughs]

830
00:45:36.984 --> 00:45:38.694
-Ooh!
-Pretty, aren't they?

831
00:45:38.777 --> 00:45:39.820
[gasps] Ooh!

832
00:45:41.947 --> 00:45:43.907
This looks familiar.

833
00:45:43.991 --> 00:45:45.701
Like something I saw in the Mangunrok.

834
00:45:45.784 --> 00:45:47.661
[laughs] That'll be ten coins.

835
00:45:47.744 --> 00:45:50.956
[chuckles] Oh, no, I'll pass for now.

836
00:45:51.039 --> 00:45:53.125
[merchants chattering]

837
00:45:54.293 --> 00:45:55.335
[worker] Again!

838
00:45:56.170 --> 00:45:57.337
Again!

839
00:45:58.422 --> 00:45:59.590
Again.

840
00:46:00.382 --> 00:46:02.301
Oh, here it is. Okay.

841
00:46:02.885 --> 00:46:04.219
I'll take that.

842
00:46:04.303 --> 00:46:05.429
Thank you so much.

843
00:46:06.221 --> 00:46:07.473
I shall return shortly.

844
00:46:07.556 --> 00:46:09.391
I have something to see to.

845
00:46:09.475 --> 00:46:11.935
Okay. Let's meet
in front of this place later.

846
00:46:12.519 --> 00:46:14.146
[sighs] Just a moment.

847
00:46:17.065 --> 00:46:18.317
No thanks.

848
00:46:19.151 --> 00:46:20.736
I already have money.

849
00:46:21.361 --> 00:46:22.779
[sighs]

850
00:46:24.656 --> 00:46:26.200
Put your money away.

851
00:46:26.283 --> 00:46:28.744
Uh, you don't need to do this.

852
00:46:29.953 --> 00:46:30.996
Be right back.

853
00:46:33.790 --> 00:46:36.293
[miller] I've never ground
anything like this before.

854
00:46:37.461 --> 00:46:38.712
[sniffs, gags]

855
00:46:38.795 --> 00:46:40.255
It's so strong! Is it a pepper?

856
00:46:40.339 --> 00:46:41.965
Yes, they're called chilies.

857
00:46:42.049 --> 00:46:44.468
I've found they can be pretty hard
to grind up due to their heat.

858
00:46:44.551 --> 00:46:46.303
So please take good care of it, okay?

859
00:46:46.386 --> 00:46:48.805
Of course. That's five coins.

860
00:46:48.889 --> 00:46:50.182
It… it's five coins?

861
00:46:50.265 --> 00:46:53.143
I-I heard it's only two coins though.

862
00:46:54.436 --> 00:46:57.523
Damn, if I hadn't taken this
it would've been a disaster.

863
00:46:58.106 --> 00:47:00.317
Maybe next time I could get a discount.

864
00:47:00.400 --> 00:47:01.818
Take good care of it, okay?

865
00:47:01.902 --> 00:47:02.986
[worker] Again!

866
00:47:09.284 --> 00:47:10.285
Give me that one.

867
00:47:13.121 --> 00:47:14.831
-We'll take all of them.
-[merchant gasps]

868
00:47:32.307 --> 00:47:34.434
[sighs] Where is he?

869
00:47:34.518 --> 00:47:36.812
What on earth could be taking so long?

870
00:47:38.188 --> 00:47:39.648
Where'd he even go?

871
00:47:41.441 --> 00:47:43.944
I could explore a little bit.

872
00:47:44.027 --> 00:47:45.028
Hmm.

873
00:47:46.905 --> 00:47:48.156
A quick look won't hurt.

874
00:47:55.956 --> 00:47:57.207
What is this?

875
00:47:57.291 --> 00:47:59.668
Do you think
the chief royal cook is still inside?

876
00:47:59.751 --> 00:48:01.795
I will go check on her, Your Majesty.

877
00:48:02.588 --> 00:48:03.714
Yes, do that.

878
00:48:09.970 --> 00:48:11.805
[wind howls]

879
00:48:17.519 --> 00:48:19.187
[thunder rumbling]

880
00:48:21.273 --> 00:48:22.608
[Gil-geum groans]

881
00:48:22.691 --> 00:48:25.736
It's a sun shower. What do we do?
Hurry! Don't let them get wet!

882
00:48:25.819 --> 00:48:27.738
What, is there a tiger
getting married today?

883
00:48:27.821 --> 00:48:30.240
Well isn't this just a lovely day.
Oh my, oh my!

884
00:48:30.324 --> 00:48:31.658
[screams]

885
00:48:31.742 --> 00:48:32.784
Uh…

886
00:48:32.868 --> 00:48:35.203
Hey, those are precious ingredients,
you can't…

887
00:48:41.209 --> 00:48:42.586
[in Mandarin] That sure is potent.

888
00:48:43.295 --> 00:48:45.380
What is this scent?

889
00:48:53.347 --> 00:48:54.848
[in English] Who exactly are you?

890
00:48:54.931 --> 00:48:57.351
Our kitchen is not open to just anyone.

891
00:48:57.434 --> 00:48:59.811
This is one of the Ming cooks, Ya Feixiu.

892
00:48:59.895 --> 00:49:01.688
Huh? [stammers] A Ming cook?

893
00:49:02.731 --> 00:49:06.610
[stammers] Cook Maeng!
Cook Eom! Come quick! [shouts]

894
00:49:07.986 --> 00:49:12.449
Ah, it would start raining today.
Hey, Hwang, hold this down.

895
00:49:12.532 --> 00:49:13.617
Yes, sir.

896
00:49:13.700 --> 00:49:15.118
-Cook Min.
-Yes?

897
00:49:15.202 --> 00:49:17.454
I'd say your green onion
chopping skills have improved.

898
00:49:17.537 --> 00:49:19.122
Thank you for noticing. [chuckles]

899
00:49:19.206 --> 00:49:20.957
[Gil-geum] Hey! Come quickly!

900
00:49:21.041 --> 00:49:24.920
I didn't know she…The Ming Cook took
the chili pepper. She… [imitates bite]

901
00:49:25.003 --> 00:49:27.214
-I tried, but she didn't…
-You'll choke if you don't slow down.

902
00:49:27.297 --> 00:49:29.257
-Would you spit it out already?
-[groans]

903
00:49:29.341 --> 00:49:32.719
She's the cook from Ming. She's here!
She's in the royal kitchen!

904
00:49:48.777 --> 00:49:50.195
[clears throat]

905
00:49:51.071 --> 00:49:54.783
I am called Eom. A royal cook.

906
00:49:57.953 --> 00:50:00.789
[speaks Mandarin]

907
00:50:00.872 --> 00:50:02.499
[in English] Mmm, what did she say?

908
00:50:02.582 --> 00:50:05.043
-She complimented your knife skills.
-Ah.

909
00:50:05.127 --> 00:50:07.462
She said his skills were pitiful,
did she not?

910
00:50:07.546 --> 00:50:09.756
You thought I wouldn't understand her?

911
00:50:09.840 --> 00:50:11.174
What?

912
00:50:15.011 --> 00:50:18.765
Why so much disrespect
from a visitor to our kitchen?

913
00:50:18.849 --> 00:50:20.976
Tsk. [in Mandarin] What a mess.

914
00:50:21.059 --> 00:50:22.144
[in English] He's talking to you!

915
00:50:22.227 --> 00:50:25.522
Cook Eom, I've spent over ten years
chopping in this kitchen.

916
00:50:25.605 --> 00:50:26.606
I won't stand for this.

917
00:50:26.690 --> 00:50:28.525
Move aside. I won't let her insult us.

918
00:50:28.608 --> 00:50:31.695
What? Should we have a green onion
chopping contest or something? Huh?

919
00:50:31.778 --> 00:50:34.823
[clears throat]
Now, now, now, just settle down.

920
00:50:34.906 --> 00:50:37.659
She's… she's on the envoy delegation.

921
00:50:37.743 --> 00:50:39.911
[in Mandarin] How about
a green onion chopping competition?

922
00:50:40.579 --> 00:50:42.622
A chopping contest? [scoffs]

923
00:50:42.706 --> 00:50:44.916
With such pitiful knife skills?

924
00:50:45.000 --> 00:50:47.836
[in English] "Pitiful knife skills"?
Watch what you say!

925
00:50:47.919 --> 00:50:52.257
They say that even a stay dog deserves
respect but she isn't deserving of any!

926
00:50:52.340 --> 00:50:53.633
Don't talk out of turn.

927
00:50:53.717 --> 00:50:54.885
[in Mandarin] You are so noisy.

928
00:50:56.219 --> 00:51:00.098
They say an empty cart
rattles the loudest.

929
00:51:01.141 --> 00:51:02.768
[speaks Mandarin]

930
00:51:02.851 --> 00:51:04.478
[in English]
Where is the chief royal cook?

931
00:51:04.561 --> 00:51:05.687
The chief royal cook?

932
00:51:05.771 --> 00:51:07.939
[scoffs] I'm your challenger.

933
00:51:08.023 --> 00:51:09.858
Stop disrespecting my seniors.

934
00:51:09.941 --> 00:51:11.860
We'll settle this right now, you and I.

935
00:51:11.943 --> 00:51:13.320
[speaking Mandarin]

936
00:51:13.403 --> 00:51:14.696
How ridiculous.

937
00:51:15.655 --> 00:51:17.657
-Are you all…
-[shouts]

938
00:51:19.242 --> 00:51:20.827
[cooks gasping]

939
00:51:23.121 --> 00:51:25.165
…sure about this?

940
00:51:25.248 --> 00:51:26.917
[gasps]

941
00:51:29.836 --> 00:51:33.256
[in English] Cook Min.
Are… Are you really sure?

942
00:51:34.257 --> 00:51:36.843
Cook Maeng has excellent knife skills.
He can handle this.

943
00:51:36.927 --> 00:51:38.762
It'll be less pressure.

944
00:51:38.845 --> 00:51:42.057
I think she's actually one of
their junior cooks, from the looks of her.

945
00:51:42.140 --> 00:51:45.936
It'll be better for us
if he is the one to handle this. Right?

946
00:51:48.647 --> 00:51:52.526
Cook Min, don't worry about speed,
what's critical is that you chop evenly.

947
00:51:53.151 --> 00:51:54.361
I will keep that in mind.

948
00:51:54.444 --> 00:51:57.197
[Gil-geum] You can do it.
We're counting on you, Cook Min, okay?

949
00:52:04.329 --> 00:52:05.622
[Yi Heon sighs]

950
00:52:07.082 --> 00:52:10.502
The chief royal cook doesn't know these
parts well. Where could she have gone?

951
00:52:10.585 --> 00:52:12.003
[Su-hyeok] Apologies, Your Majesty.

952
00:52:12.087 --> 00:52:14.714
I will check the upper path.
I should have checked it earlier.

953
00:52:14.798 --> 00:52:16.091
Do that.

954
00:52:16.174 --> 00:52:19.719
I shall wait here then,
in case you let her slip past.

955
00:52:19.803 --> 00:52:20.887
Yes, Your Majesty.

956
00:52:27.686 --> 00:52:30.272
[gentle music playing]

957
00:52:57.173 --> 00:52:59.426
You're back. [breathing heavily]

958
00:52:59.509 --> 00:53:01.052
Where on earth did you run off to?

959
00:53:01.136 --> 00:53:03.263
I thought I'd go get flowers
while I waited.

960
00:53:03.346 --> 00:53:05.891
I'm glad to see that
the rain did not hinder you.

961
00:53:06.725 --> 00:53:08.226
And, what is that?

962
00:53:09.102 --> 00:53:10.729
Oh, irises.

963
00:53:10.812 --> 00:53:13.398
It's a flower that's used
to help ease your stress.

964
00:53:13.481 --> 00:53:15.358
Irises?

965
00:53:16.985 --> 00:53:18.069
Hmm.

966
00:53:19.905 --> 00:53:20.906
[chuckles]

967
00:53:21.740 --> 00:53:22.991
It is called butkkot.

968
00:53:23.992 --> 00:53:25.076
"Butkkot"?

969
00:53:26.202 --> 00:53:27.287
[gasps]

970
00:53:27.370 --> 00:53:28.538
[Ji-young screams]

971
00:53:32.834 --> 00:53:33.877
[gasps]

972
00:53:33.960 --> 00:53:35.795
[romantic music playing]

973
00:53:42.260 --> 00:53:45.138
[gasps] My flowers. Ah!

974
00:53:45.221 --> 00:53:47.223
Oh, they're ruined.

975
00:53:48.266 --> 00:53:50.644
I will get you better ones.

976
00:53:51.686 --> 00:53:53.980
Enough, let us go.

977
00:53:54.648 --> 00:53:55.690
[sighs]

978
00:53:57.859 --> 00:53:58.985
Hang on.

979
00:54:00.820 --> 00:54:03.323
I said it we have to leave,
why are you dallying?

980
00:54:03.406 --> 00:54:04.532
I'm coming, okay?

981
00:54:05.325 --> 00:54:06.368
[sighs]

982
00:54:09.746 --> 00:54:11.665
Do not pick them up, they are in the dirt.

983
00:54:11.748 --> 00:54:14.584
You do know I got them for you, right?

984
00:54:14.668 --> 00:54:16.002
They can be used as medicine.

985
00:54:16.086 --> 00:54:19.130
And they help to calm your mind,
so you should keep them in your room.

986
00:54:19.214 --> 00:54:20.298
[scoffs]

987
00:54:21.007 --> 00:54:23.677
Like a mouse being nursed by a cat.

988
00:54:23.760 --> 00:54:24.928
The competition is near.

989
00:54:25.011 --> 00:54:27.639
I wanted to plant them in the Jangwonseo.

990
00:54:36.314 --> 00:54:37.315
[Yi Heon grunts]

991
00:54:59.462 --> 00:55:00.463
Your Maje…

992
00:55:03.216 --> 00:55:04.259
[clears throat]

993
00:55:06.594 --> 00:55:07.595
[both sigh]

994
00:55:09.639 --> 00:55:10.974
[sniffles]

995
00:55:11.516 --> 00:55:13.309
[chuckles]

996
00:55:13.393 --> 00:55:15.770
Your Majesty. Your face.

997
00:55:15.854 --> 00:55:17.397
Hmm?

998
00:55:17.480 --> 00:55:19.441
[chuckles, clears throat]

999
00:55:20.692 --> 00:55:22.027
Right here.

1000
00:55:23.737 --> 00:55:24.904
[chuckles]

1001
00:55:26.239 --> 00:55:27.449
Wait, what did you just do?

1002
00:55:28.783 --> 00:55:29.784
I just…

1003
00:55:29.868 --> 00:55:32.370
You had something on your face, so…

1004
00:55:34.622 --> 00:55:37.208
Well, there's something
on your face as well.

1005
00:55:38.251 --> 00:55:39.627
[laughing]

1006
00:55:41.296 --> 00:55:43.048
Cut it out, seriously.

1007
00:55:43.131 --> 00:55:45.008
-Why? Come here. Hey!
-Stop it!

1008
00:55:45.091 --> 00:55:48.094
-Stop it, stop it! [huffs]
-Wait, come back. [laughs]

1009
00:55:48.178 --> 00:55:49.763
Why are you running away? Come back!

1010
00:55:52.682 --> 00:55:56.770
I didn't think it was possible
for your face to get even uglier.

1011
00:55:56.853 --> 00:55:59.773
[scoffs] Oh wow, my deepest apologies.

1012
00:56:00.607 --> 00:56:02.567
You're not looking much better,
Your Majesty.

1013
00:56:02.650 --> 00:56:04.319
What? [scoffs]

1014
00:56:05.403 --> 00:56:06.571
[Yi Heon clears throat]

1015
00:56:06.654 --> 00:56:09.032
Owing to the fact
that you presented this gift,

1016
00:56:09.657 --> 00:56:11.910
I shall make an exception
and overlook your impudence this once.

1017
00:56:11.993 --> 00:56:15.288
Well, I'm grateful that you
were pleased by the flowers.

1018
00:56:17.082 --> 00:56:20.835
Is it really okay that you spend
so much time away from your duties?

1019
00:56:21.544 --> 00:56:23.379
Of course. There's nothing more important

1020
00:56:23.463 --> 00:56:26.341
than preparing the materials
for the upcoming contest.

1021
00:56:26.925 --> 00:56:29.135
[sighs] Yes, that is true.

1022
00:56:30.512 --> 00:56:31.554
But…

1023
00:56:32.180 --> 00:56:35.433
Are you sure chili peppers
will win the competition for us?

1024
00:56:35.517 --> 00:56:38.228
[inhales] Nothing can be truly guaranteed,

1025
00:56:38.311 --> 00:56:40.939
but our best bet is to go in guns blazing.

1026
00:56:41.022 --> 00:56:44.609
The chili and gochujang
are going to be secret ingredients,

1027
00:56:44.692 --> 00:56:46.611
giving us an advantage.

1028
00:56:46.694 --> 00:56:49.489
Oh, you should remember
that taste as well, Your Majesty.

1029
00:56:49.572 --> 00:56:51.324
It's the same as the bibimbap we had.

1030
00:56:53.660 --> 00:56:54.744
Ah.

1031
00:56:56.454 --> 00:56:58.081
[coughing]

1032
00:56:58.748 --> 00:57:00.875
Ah, that tear-inducing taste?

1033
00:57:00.959 --> 00:57:02.627
[laughs] Yes.

1034
00:57:03.128 --> 00:57:07.006
Uh, well. I'll be in the royal kitchen,
if you need me. Good night.

1035
00:57:07.090 --> 00:57:09.843
Wait. Give me your hand.

1036
00:57:09.926 --> 00:57:11.678
Huh? My hand?

1037
00:57:17.934 --> 00:57:21.062
I was looking at this in the shop earlier.

1038
00:57:21.146 --> 00:57:23.231
It seemed like you wanted it.

1039
00:57:23.898 --> 00:57:25.066
[Ji-young] No way.

1040
00:57:25.150 --> 00:57:27.902
Did he see me
admiring this at the market?

1041
00:57:30.738 --> 00:57:32.991
I shall take my leave. [clears throat]

1042
00:57:37.954 --> 00:57:39.247
[screams]

1043
00:57:45.920 --> 00:57:47.589
[Su-hyeok clears throat]

1044
00:57:48.715 --> 00:57:49.716
Oh, right.

1045
00:57:52.719 --> 00:57:56.473
[straining] Would it kill you
to help me bring these inside?

1046
00:58:14.324 --> 00:58:15.658
[Yi Heon] Butkkot.

1047
00:58:19.162 --> 00:58:20.747
Butkkot…

1048
00:58:44.437 --> 00:58:47.899
How am I going to face him again
if I lose this competition?

1049
00:58:50.235 --> 00:58:51.528
[sighs]

1050
00:59:02.413 --> 00:59:04.040
[groans] Are you okay?

1051
00:59:04.707 --> 00:59:06.042
Huh?

1052
00:59:06.626 --> 00:59:08.461
You're the cook from Ming?

1053
00:59:08.545 --> 00:59:11.214
[in Mandarin] Joseon's chief royal cook.

1054
00:59:11.297 --> 00:59:13.967
[in English] Uh… What brings you here?

1055
00:59:14.050 --> 00:59:17.095
[in Mandarin] You got lucky today.

1056
00:59:19.430 --> 00:59:21.182
[laughs, speaks English]
You should hurry up.

1057
00:59:21.266 --> 00:59:24.435
Your colleagues are eager to see you.
[laughing]

1058
00:59:28.106 --> 00:59:29.107
[gasps]

1059
00:59:29.732 --> 00:59:30.733
What the…

1060
00:59:32.110 --> 00:59:34.153
What on earth is going on in here?

1061
00:59:34.237 --> 00:59:37.991
[crying] Oh, heavens, oh, goodness.

1062
00:59:38.074 --> 00:59:41.911
It's awful, miss. They came
and they were judging us!

1063
00:59:41.995 --> 00:59:43.746
Okay. It's all right, breathe.

1064
00:59:43.830 --> 00:59:45.206
Tell me slowly.

1065
00:59:45.290 --> 00:59:47.584
Okay. That Ya Feixiu girl,

1066
00:59:47.667 --> 00:59:50.878
she showed us how incredible
her skills really are.

1067
00:59:50.962 --> 00:59:54.007
She had a green onion
chopping contest with Cook Min…

1068
00:59:59.095 --> 01:00:02.181
[Min] She has the unwavering focus
of a Shaolin master.

1069
01:00:02.265 --> 01:00:04.017
It was a masterful showing.

1070
01:00:04.100 --> 01:00:05.476
Ah!

1071
01:00:05.560 --> 01:00:07.562
[Bong-sik] That wasn't the only mistake.

1072
01:00:07.645 --> 01:00:11.441
[Sim] If I'm being honest,
I've always been a bit scared of knives…

1073
01:00:17.030 --> 01:00:18.114
[groans]

1074
01:00:20.199 --> 01:00:22.744
[Bong-sik] She made me feel so anxious,

1075
01:00:22.827 --> 01:00:25.997
I ended up chopping
inedible parts of the onion.

1076
01:00:26.080 --> 01:00:30.918
But I never thought
that Cook Maeng would lose.

1077
01:00:39.594 --> 01:00:40.595
[breathing heavily]

1078
01:00:48.728 --> 01:00:50.271
[panting]

1079
01:00:52.440 --> 01:00:56.903
It's the first time anyone
has outpaced me in a contest of speed.

1080
01:00:56.986 --> 01:01:00.198
Are you saying
nobody here won a single match?

1081
01:01:00.281 --> 01:01:02.992
There is no excuse, we all failed.

1082
01:01:03.076 --> 01:01:05.912
[Gil-geum]
What are we supposed to do, miss? [sighs]

1083
01:01:06.537 --> 01:01:07.914
[scoffs]

1084
01:01:10.208 --> 01:01:11.334
[chuckles]

1085
01:01:11.918 --> 01:01:13.795
Is she trying to declare a war?

1086
01:01:13.878 --> 01:01:16.881
What kind of person goes into someone
else's kitchen and behaves that way?

1087
01:01:17.632 --> 01:01:18.841
Ah, jeez.

1088
01:01:20.760 --> 01:01:23.513
And what is so important
about learning to chop quickly

1089
01:01:23.596 --> 01:01:25.556
if you never learned human decency.

1090
01:01:25.640 --> 01:01:28.226
I can tell everything about her
by how she chops.

1091
01:01:28.309 --> 01:01:31.813
It's all just for show,
I'm not seeing any artistry here. [scoffs]

1092
01:01:32.814 --> 01:01:33.815
[sighs]

1093
01:01:35.191 --> 01:01:37.276
[scoffs]
Are you all going to give up so easily?

1094
01:01:37.360 --> 01:01:39.487
They came into our kitchen
and made a mess!

1095
01:01:39.570 --> 01:01:41.197
We need to teach them a lesson.

1096
01:01:41.280 --> 01:01:43.574
Are we going to let them
disrespect the cooks of Joseon?

1097
01:01:43.658 --> 01:01:44.992
Well?

1098
01:01:46.744 --> 01:01:48.037
Hmm?

1099
01:01:48.121 --> 01:01:49.288
[Bong-sik] Okay.

1100
01:01:49.872 --> 01:01:52.333
Screw it, I say we go to war!

1101
01:01:52.417 --> 01:01:54.544
[whimpers] I'll never lose again!

1102
01:01:54.627 --> 01:01:56.587
The next time I go up against her,

1103
01:01:56.671 --> 01:01:59.215
I'll show her what it means
to really chop with precision.

1104
01:02:00.091 --> 01:02:02.885
I'm with you. I'll give it another try.

1105
01:02:03.469 --> 01:02:06.889
Miss, you just say the word,
and I will do whatever I can!

1106
01:02:06.973 --> 01:02:09.058
Us, too! We'll also lend our strength!

1107
01:02:09.142 --> 01:02:11.060
-We'll also help!
-We'll also help!

1108
01:02:11.144 --> 01:02:13.187
-[clamoring]
-Us too!

1109
01:02:13.271 --> 01:02:14.564
We can help too!

1110
01:02:14.647 --> 01:02:16.983
All right, all right, all right,
all right, all right!

1111
01:02:17.066 --> 01:02:18.693
Now come on, fighting!

1112
01:02:18.776 --> 01:02:20.528
-Fi… What?
-Uh…

1113
01:02:20.611 --> 01:02:22.530
-What?
-Uh…

1114
01:02:23.573 --> 01:02:24.615
Uh…

1115
01:02:26.617 --> 01:02:28.077
Royal Kitchen, let's rise!

1116
01:02:28.161 --> 01:02:30.413
[all] Royal Kitchen, let's rise!

1117
01:02:30.496 --> 01:02:31.748
Royal Kitchen, let's fight!

1118
01:02:31.831 --> 01:02:33.791
[all] Royal Kitchen, let's fight!

1119
01:02:33.875 --> 01:02:35.293
Royal Kitchen, let's win!

1120
01:02:35.376 --> 01:02:37.754
[all] Royal Kitchen, let's win!

1121
01:02:37.837 --> 01:02:39.380
[cheering]

1122
01:02:42.967 --> 01:02:46.137
[in Mandarin]
So how were the Joseon cooks?

1123
01:02:46.220 --> 01:02:48.723
I competed with them
in a green onion chopping competition,

1124
01:02:48.806 --> 01:02:51.142
and their basic knife skills
were pathetic.

1125
01:02:51.225 --> 01:02:53.478
What about the chief royal cook?

1126
01:02:53.561 --> 01:02:56.355
She was not there.

1127
01:02:57.023 --> 01:02:59.358
You wasted time playing with the minions.

1128
01:03:00.026 --> 01:03:02.361
Not entirely.

1129
01:03:03.613 --> 01:03:09.911
I found out they have
a special seasoning ingredient.

1130
01:03:11.829 --> 01:03:13.080
What is this?

1131
01:03:15.833 --> 01:03:19.170
It smells like mala, but it is different.

1132
01:03:24.717 --> 01:03:29.388
[scoffs] I guess we will find out
when the competition begins.

1133
01:03:32.558 --> 01:03:35.853
I am very curious to see

1134
01:03:35.937 --> 01:03:40.775
what is making the Joseon king
so confident.

1135
01:03:47.657 --> 01:03:50.201
[in English] I understand her skills
in the kitchen are extraordinary,

1136
01:03:50.284 --> 01:03:53.204
but to put the fate of our nation
on the line for a competition?

1137
01:03:53.287 --> 01:03:56.332
The Ming envoy traveled here
with three cooks.

1138
01:03:56.415 --> 01:03:58.793
It's clear this was their idea
from the start.

1139
01:03:58.876 --> 01:04:02.463
Her Royal Highness is conceiving
a new arrangement,

1140
01:04:02.547 --> 01:04:04.298
so do not worry so much.

1141
01:04:05.341 --> 01:04:11.931
My son, if we lose this competition, His
Majesty's dignity will be forever stained.

1142
01:04:12.014 --> 01:04:15.184
Tell me do you have
some clever trick up your sleeve?

1143
01:04:15.268 --> 01:04:16.269
Father.

1144
01:04:16.978 --> 01:04:18.479
You worry far too much.

1145
01:04:19.564 --> 01:04:23.067
Their skills do not concern me
so long as we are on Joseon soil.

1146
01:04:24.277 --> 01:04:27.280
Under no circumstances
will they be allowed to have their way.

1147
01:04:27.363 --> 01:04:29.282
I will never stand for it.

1148
01:04:31.367 --> 01:04:33.160
[laughing]

1149
01:04:43.838 --> 01:04:45.047
SWEET

1150
01:04:52.722 --> 01:04:54.265
MEAT

1151
01:04:55.016 --> 01:04:56.017
FISH

1152
01:05:03.858 --> 01:05:07.862
[speaking Mandarin]

1153
01:05:07.945 --> 01:05:09.488
[in English] He asks you to choose first.

1154
01:05:09.572 --> 01:05:10.573
No.

1155
01:05:11.741 --> 01:05:13.492
I think the chief envoy
should choose first.

1156
01:05:13.576 --> 01:05:15.661
[speaking Mandarin]

1157
01:05:18.581 --> 01:05:21.250
[English translator] He asks if choosing
at the same time is acceptable?

1158
01:05:21.918 --> 01:05:22.919
Of course.

1159
01:05:23.002 --> 01:05:24.837
-[translator 2 speaks Mandarin]
-[grunts]

1160
01:05:40.186 --> 01:05:44.315
-"Mu" for nothingness, and "yuk" for meat.
-"Mu" for nothingness, and "yuk" for meat.

1161
01:05:46.943 --> 01:05:48.653
So for their first dish,

1162
01:05:49.362 --> 01:05:52.239
I expect a meat dish
that has never been seen before.

1163
01:05:53.157 --> 01:05:56.953
[in Mandarin] Correct.
A meat dish the world has never seen.

1164
01:05:57.620 --> 01:06:00.039
[muttering]

1165
01:06:05.878 --> 01:06:09.006
[in English] I think you should
choose next, Chief Royal Cook.

1166
01:06:10.341 --> 01:06:11.467
What?

1167
01:06:11.550 --> 01:06:13.052
You're sure?

1168
01:06:13.678 --> 01:06:14.679
Yes.

1169
01:06:18.766 --> 01:06:20.017
Bailong.

1170
01:06:21.852 --> 01:06:23.312
[in Mandarin] Yes, my lord.

1171
01:06:48.337 --> 01:06:50.297
[in English] Ji, for "knowledge,"
and yeok for "change."

1172
01:06:50.381 --> 01:06:52.800
Ji, for "knowledge,"
and yeok for "change."

1173
01:06:52.883 --> 01:06:54.552
[exclaims]

1174
01:06:55.136 --> 01:06:57.263
Interesting, to both know and change.

1175
01:06:57.346 --> 01:06:59.056
[speaking Mandarin]

1176
01:07:02.393 --> 01:07:04.270
[English translator]
He suggests that we draw again.

1177
01:07:04.353 --> 01:07:06.605
To know, but really to change…

1178
01:07:08.315 --> 01:07:09.483
[chuckles]

1179
01:07:11.110 --> 01:07:15.531
Diplomacy is fostering an understanding
of each other's cultures.

1180
01:07:16.323 --> 01:07:17.366
In that spirit,

1181
01:07:18.075 --> 01:07:20.578
I suggest each cook
makes the others native dish.

1182
01:07:20.661 --> 01:07:22.204
[translator 2 speaking Mandarin]

1183
01:07:22.288 --> 01:07:24.415
Are you suggesting
that for the second round,

1184
01:07:24.498 --> 01:07:27.626
-the Ming cooks are to make a Joseon dish…
-[English translator continues]

1185
01:07:27.710 --> 01:07:30.129
…and the Joseon cooks
are to make a Ming dish?

1186
01:07:30.963 --> 01:07:33.299
-[in English] That is correct.
-[translator 2 speaks Mandarin]

1187
01:07:33.382 --> 01:07:36.385
[laughs, speaks Mandarin]
What an interesting idea.

1188
01:07:38.304 --> 01:07:40.306
[Ji-young, in English]
Why is he so confident?

1189
01:07:40.389 --> 01:07:42.767
Are his cooks proficient
in Joseon cuisine as well?

1190
01:07:42.850 --> 01:07:45.811
Well then, all that remains
is the last dish.

1191
01:07:47.480 --> 01:07:48.564
[sighs]

1192
01:07:50.191 --> 01:07:51.400
[chuckles]

1193
01:07:53.861 --> 01:07:55.946
Uncle, would you like to draw one?

1194
01:07:58.240 --> 01:07:59.408
Your Highness.

1195
01:07:59.992 --> 01:08:01.744
-Your Highness.
-[startles]

1196
01:08:01.827 --> 01:08:03.412
-Huh?
-He asks you to draw.

1197
01:08:03.496 --> 01:08:04.914
What?

1198
01:08:05.498 --> 01:08:07.666
Ah. [clears throat] Ah, yes.

1199
01:08:07.750 --> 01:08:08.834
You… You want me?

1200
01:08:08.918 --> 01:08:11.796
Yes. You are Saongwon's superintendent.

1201
01:08:12.588 --> 01:08:14.298
You should pick the final theme.

1202
01:08:14.381 --> 01:08:17.843
[coughs] Of course, Your Majesty.
[chuckles]

1203
01:08:17.927 --> 01:08:21.472
I live for the anticipation
of the draw. [grunts]

1204
01:08:21.555 --> 01:08:22.598
Kong Wenli.

1205
01:08:23.349 --> 01:08:24.725
[in Mandarin] Yes, my lord.

1206
01:08:28.145 --> 01:08:29.730
[Jesan, in English] Let's see…

1207
01:08:42.326 --> 01:08:44.495
Tang, for "broth," sam, for "ginseng."

1208
01:08:44.578 --> 01:08:47.456
Tang, for "broth," sam, for "ginseng."

1209
01:08:47.540 --> 01:08:49.083
[exclaims]

1210
01:08:49.166 --> 01:08:51.085
[chuckles]

1211
01:08:51.168 --> 01:08:54.296
They can not be rivaled,
where soup is involved.

1212
01:08:54.880 --> 01:08:56.882
[Won-jun]
This is going to be quite a challenge.

1213
01:08:56.966 --> 01:08:58.134
I agree with you.

1214
01:09:00.344 --> 01:09:02.221
Soup and ginseng…

1215
01:09:02.304 --> 01:09:05.516
[laughs, speaks in Mandarin]
I see we have soup.

1216
01:09:07.768 --> 01:09:11.856
[in English] It appears the final dish
is soup with ginseng in it.

1217
01:09:16.318 --> 01:09:18.529
[sighs, speaks Mandarin]

1218
01:09:22.616 --> 01:09:24.785
[English translator] He suggests
raising the stakes of the wager

1219
01:09:24.869 --> 01:09:26.579
now that the dishes have been arranged.

1220
01:09:28.914 --> 01:09:31.542
You want to raise the stake of our wager?

1221
01:09:32.459 --> 01:09:33.627
[chuckles]

1222
01:09:34.753 --> 01:09:36.088
What might you have in mind?

1223
01:09:36.172 --> 01:09:38.007
[speaks Mandarin]

1224
01:09:44.889 --> 01:09:48.017
[English translator] He requests adding
100 tribute women to the usual amount

1225
01:09:48.100 --> 01:09:50.144
and the mining rights
to ginseng in Joseon.

1226
01:09:50.227 --> 01:09:52.104
-[clamoring]
-That's an outrage!

1227
01:10:01.405 --> 01:10:02.531
[sighs]

1228
01:10:03.240 --> 01:10:04.283
Well then.

1229
01:10:05.284 --> 01:10:07.244
We too, have additional conditions.

1230
01:10:07.328 --> 01:10:08.996
[translator 2 speaks Mandarin]

1231
01:10:10.664 --> 01:10:12.333
[in English] If Joseon wins,

1232
01:10:12.416 --> 01:10:15.127
Ming will only get half the tributes
that were paid in the past.

1233
01:10:15.211 --> 01:10:17.213
Furthermore, Joseon will be allowed

1234
01:10:17.296 --> 01:10:20.299
to prepurchase all that we require
in jinmal and cane sugar.

1235
01:10:20.382 --> 01:10:22.009
[translator 2 speaks Mandarin]

1236
01:10:24.178 --> 01:10:28.724
As much flour as they wish?

1237
01:10:28.807 --> 01:10:30.226
[grumbling]

1238
01:10:31.852 --> 01:10:34.063
How is this any different
from asking our great nation

1239
01:10:34.146 --> 01:10:35.522
to pay tribute to Joseon instead?

1240
01:10:35.606 --> 01:10:36.941
[laughs]

1241
01:10:38.234 --> 01:10:40.569
[in English] What? Are you nervous?

1242
01:10:40.653 --> 01:10:42.863
-[translator 2 speaks Mandarin]
-[speaks Mandarin]

1243
01:10:42.947 --> 01:10:45.616
[English translator] This matter requires
the opinion of His Majesty the Emperor

1244
01:10:45.699 --> 01:10:47.409
and the court.

1245
01:10:47.493 --> 01:10:50.162
It is not a matter
that he can decide on his own.

1246
01:10:51.664 --> 01:10:53.832
I suppose the wager
shall stay the same then.

1247
01:10:53.916 --> 01:10:56.252
[translator 2 speaks Mandarin]

1248
01:10:57.628 --> 01:10:59.255
[speaks Mandarin]

1249
01:11:03.926 --> 01:11:06.053
[English translator]
He says he promises to strongly petition

1250
01:11:06.136 --> 01:11:08.222
His Majesty the Emperor if Ming loses.

1251
01:11:08.847 --> 01:11:09.848
[laughs]

1252
01:11:10.599 --> 01:11:11.850
Very well.

1253
01:11:11.934 --> 01:11:15.646
Chief Royal Secretary, record today's
discussions with the envoy in writing.

1254
01:11:15.729 --> 01:11:18.482
The cooks of both countries
will compete in three rounds,

1255
01:11:18.565 --> 01:11:20.276
and the competition will last one sijin.

1256
01:11:20.359 --> 01:11:21.360
ONE SIJIN:
APPROXIMATELY TWO HOURS

1257
01:11:21.443 --> 01:11:25.197
To decide on their dish and prepare
ingredients, each kitchen has three days.

1258
01:11:29.243 --> 01:11:33.789
Although that is not much time,
so it will be five days.

1259
01:11:33.872 --> 01:11:35.332
[translator 2 speaks Mandarin]

1260
01:11:36.125 --> 01:11:37.209
Very well.

1261
01:11:37.293 --> 01:11:40.212
Five days shall it be.

1262
01:11:40.296 --> 01:11:41.380
[in English] Very well.

1263
01:11:41.463 --> 01:11:46.218
The competition starts in five days,
at Huijeongdang, in the sheep's hour.

1264
01:11:46.302 --> 01:11:49.305
Cooks of both nations, show your respect.

1265
01:11:49.930 --> 01:11:52.850
[speaks Mandarin]

1266
01:12:06.322 --> 01:12:09.116
[in English] I think you left your cai dao
in the royal kitchen.

1267
01:12:09.199 --> 01:12:11.035
[interprets into Mandarin]

1268
01:12:12.244 --> 01:12:15.956
[in English] I left it at Taepyeonggwan.
Yeah, it's safe and sound.

1269
01:12:16.498 --> 01:12:18.667
[translator 2 speaks Mandarin]

1270
01:12:23.422 --> 01:12:24.757
[gasps]

1271
01:12:26.133 --> 01:12:27.551
How rude.

1272
01:12:28.135 --> 01:12:29.720
Is this

1273
01:12:30.304 --> 01:12:31.764
the Joseon way?

1274
01:12:34.558 --> 01:12:38.729
How dare they challenge me outright?

1275
01:12:39.772 --> 01:12:41.357
Ah…

1276
01:12:42.816 --> 01:12:44.818
They completely ruined the blade.

1277
01:12:45.486 --> 01:12:46.820
[laughs]

1278
01:12:52.493 --> 01:12:53.660
[sighs]

1279
01:13:01.960 --> 01:13:04.129
[in English] You just wait, envoys.

1280
01:13:04.922 --> 01:13:07.591
I'm going to show you blazing hot flavor.

1281
01:13:15.474 --> 01:13:17.893
PRESSURE COOKER - PACKING
COMPRESS - CAST-IRON POT

1282
01:13:38.956 --> 01:13:41.792
BON APPÉTIT, YOUR MAJESTY

1283
01:13:41.875 --> 01:13:42.876
[Ji-young] This pressure cooker.

1284
01:13:42.960 --> 01:13:46.213
There is one person in Joseon
who can make this for us.

1285
01:13:46.296 --> 01:13:48.715
[Chang-seon] He is a descendant
of Senior general Jang Yeong-sil…

1286
01:13:48.799 --> 01:13:51.260
In that case,
it is only right that I join you.

1287
01:13:51.343 --> 01:13:53.554
-I can barely stand anymore.
-[Ji-young] He's so obnoxious.

1288
01:13:53.637 --> 01:13:54.721
Your Majesty, please!

1289
01:13:54.805 --> 01:13:56.140
That's gonna explode!

1290
01:13:56.223 --> 01:13:58.475
-Let's go right now.
-What a lunatic! You'll be sorry for this.

1291
01:13:58.559 --> 01:14:00.978
[Jesan] So His Majesty
has left the palace once again.

1292
01:14:01.061 --> 01:14:05.232
There are many dangers
beyond these palace walls, are there not?

1293
01:14:05.315 --> 01:14:06.900
-The target is…
-[screams]

1294
01:14:06.984 --> 01:14:08.402
-…Chief Royal Cook Yeon.
-[swords slices]

1295
01:14:08.485 --> 01:14:10.612
[Yi Heon] Cook Yeon! Cook Yeon!

